{"timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:44:23.335Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"publish-to-curseforge","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"# CurseForge Publishing — Sia's Workshop\n\nHow to get this mod published on CurseForge. Researched 2026-10-09 against current CurseForge\nsupport docs for the v1.0.0 release (MC 1.21.1 NeoForge 21.1.x + MC 1.20.1 NeoForge 47.1.x).\nTracked by initiative `publish-to-curseforge`.\n\n## The pipeline at a glance\n\nCreate project (web) → upload a file → moderation review → live. There is no separate\n\"author\" approval gate: a registered CurseForge account can create projects at\n`authors.curseforge.com/#/projects/create/choose-game`. A new project only becomes\nvisible/syncs to the CurseForge App once it has **at least one approved Release or Beta\nfile**. Everything below assumes manual publishing through the web UI; CI automation is\ncovered at the end.\n\n## Project creation (one-time)\n\n| Field | Value for Sia's Workshop |\n| --- | --- |\n| Name | `Sia's Workshop` (must be unique on CF — will be rejected if taken) |\n| Summary | Short listing blurb, e.g. \"A compass that points away from villages, and a block that builds one — find your spot, then found your village.\" |\n| Description | Full English description (moderators reject poor grammar / insufficient description). Can be polished later. |\n| Project License | All Rights Reserved (select in dropdown; if absent, use Custom License and paste the ARR text) |\n| Class | Mods (Java) |\n| Main category | e.g. World Gen — the foundation's village generation is the headline feature |\n| Additional categories | Up to 4, only relevant ones (e.g. Map & Information for the compass, Cosmetic for cherryfy) |\n| Logo | Square 1:1 PNG (≥512×512 recommended; the CF docs don't publish exact limits). Source file lives with the designer per `docs/art/texture-specs.md`. |\n\nGallery/preview images are **not required for mods** (only texture packs/sims), but\n2–3 in-game screenshots in the description help the review and downloads.\n\n## File upload — one upload per MC version\n\nA CF file can be tagged with multiple game versions, but our jars are built per MC\nversion, so upload **two files** (from the GitHub Release\n`https://github.com/bbaaxx/siasworkshop/releases/tag/v1.0.0`):\n\n| | File 1 | File 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| File | `siasworkshop-1.21.1-1.0.0.jar` | `siasworkshop-1.20.1-1.0.0.jar` |\n| Display Name | `Sia's Workshop 1.0.0 (MC 1.21.1)` | `Sia's Workshop 1.0.0 (MC 1.20.1)` |\n| Supported Versions | `1.21.1` | `1.20.1` |\n| Modloader tag | **NeoForge** | **NeoForge** |\n| Release Type | Release (required for CF App sync + default download button) | Release |\n| Changelog | Initial release text | same |\n\n**Always set the modloader tag.** CF defaults untagged Minecraft files to Forge; the\nselector (\"Supported Modloader Versions\") is edited per file (Files tab → hover file →\nEdit). NeoForge is available as a loader tag for MC 1.20.1+ — correct for both our jars.\nDo NOT tag the 1.20.1 jar as Forge even though it sits on the Forge-compatible 47.1\nline; CF's NeoForge tag is what NeoForge-app users filter by.\n\nOther upload facts:\n\n- Minecraft mods upload as **`.jar` directly** (the \".zip only\" rule in CF docs is for\n  most *other* games). Max file size 2 GB.\n- Release Options: leave \"publish after moderation passes\" unless intentionally scheduling.\n- Related Projects: none (no dependencies, no incompatibilities known).\n- After upload the file shows **\"Under Review\"** — moderators approve it, send it back\n  with change requests, or reject (reasons are shown on the file). Same review loop\n  applies to the project itself at creation.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Project name uniqueness** — check `curseforge.com/minecraft/search` for \"Sia's\n  Workshop\" before writing the description around it.\n- **English-only, grammatical description** — explicit rejection criterion.\n- **Mac uploads**: zips made with macOS Archive contain `__macosx/` + `.ds_store` and get\n  auto-rejected. Irrelevant for direct `.jar` uploads; matters if we ever ship zip packs.\n- **Experimental project type** hides the project entirely — fine as a staging area, but\n  don't submit as experimental for the real launch (toggling back requires the legacy\n  site per CF docs).\n- \"Alpha\"-only projects don't sync to the app at all; we ship Release.\n\n## Post-publish settings worth a look\n\n- **Reward Program**: opt-in points-per-download, redeemable via PayPal/Amazon. Optional,\n  free money; decide consciously (it's a per-project toggle in the author console).\n- Source/Issue links: add the GitHub repo URL to the project page for the \"Source\" relation.\n- License display: CF shows the chosen license on the project page — matches ARR stance.\n\n## CI automation (optional follow-up)\n\nThe author console offers an **API token** (\"Creator Tools Integration — automate mod and\nfile uploads via our API through your CI/CD pipeline\"). Two common routes once we have a token:\n\n1. Direct CurseForge API `POST /projects/{projectId}/files` from `release.yml` (needs the\n   project to exist first — the API can't create projects).\n2. `mc-publish` GitHub Action (Kir-Antipov) — one action that pushes to GitHub Releases\n   (already done), CurseForge, and Modrinth; takes the CF token + project ID as inputs.\n\nRecommendation: publish v1.0.0 manually first (learn the review loop), then wire the\ntoken in once the project ID is known. Store the token as a GitHub Actions secret\n(`CURSEFORGE_TOKEN`), never in the repo.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Creating and Submitting a Project](https://support.curseforge.com/support/solutions/articles/9000197241-creating-and-submitting-a-project) (CF Support)\n- [File & Project Types and Additional Fields](https://support.curseforge.com/support/solutions/articles/9000197242-file-project-types-and-additional-fields) (CF Support)\n- [Minecraft Modloaders](https://support.curseforge.com/support/solutions/articles/9000202116-minecraft-modloaders) (CF Support)\n- [CurseForge for Mod Authors](https://authors.curseforge.com/welcome/) (creator console, API, reward program)\n- [Publishing mods with MC-Publish](https://wiki.fabricmc.net/tutorial:publishing_mods_using_github_actions) (Fabric Wiki)\n","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/curseforge-publishing.md"}}}
