{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:37:47.010Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-decision-pool-goals--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Review agents pool/board diff","prompt":"You are a read-only code reviewer for a NeoForge 1.21.1 Minecraft mod at /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop (Java 21, package root com.siaws.siawsmod). A builder subagent just implemented the \"shared decision pool + task board + comfort detectors + observation compression\" slice of an agents feature. Review the uncommitted diff for correctness and design fidelity. Do NOT edit anything.\n\n## Scope (uncommitted changes — use `git status` / `git diff`)\n\nNew files:\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/pool/PoolEntry.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/pool/AgentDecisionPool.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/tasks/BoardTask.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/tasks/TaskBoard.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/tasks/ComfortDetectors.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/AgentWorldData.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/ObservationBudget.java\n- src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/gametest/AgentsGoalsGameTest.java\n- src/main/resources/data/siasworkshop/structure/agentsgoalsgametest.empty.nbt (byte-copy of agentsgametest.empty.nbt)\n\nModified: config/Config.java, SiasWorkshop.java, content/agents/AgentObservation.java, content/agents/AgentInspectorItem.java, gametest/AgentsGameTest.java, assets/siasworkshop/lang/en_us.json\n\n## Design source of truth\n\nRead `mdocs/wiki/reference/agent-embodiment-observation.md` (Pillars 3+4 and the \"Measured budget\" section) and `AGENTS.md` (repo conventions). The agreed plan (from the initiative file `mdocs/initiatives/agents-v1-decision-pool-goals-2026-10-14--2026-10-14.md`) is: SavedData pool with schema v1, LRU cap, tag top-K retrieval, trusted-after-N-successes; task board with claim/lease/steal, lease sweep, singleton comfort deficit keys; light detector (air + solid floor + block light < threshold + cannot-see-sky); shelter detector at night (bed within radius AND skylight covered); observation budget enforcement bottom-up (ENVIRONMENT → ENTITIES → BLOCKS → PLAYERS; SELF+ACTIONS always kept) with ~chars/4 token estimator and 900-token default; inspector writes the snapshot verbatim to debug/siasworkshop/*.txt under the server game dir.\n\n## Review focus (in priority order)\n\n1. **Correctness bugs**: SavedData save/load round-trip fidelity (UUID/enum/long/int list handling, `setDirty` coverage), lease steal logic (boundary: leaseUntil == now — should be expired), claim race semantics, LRU eviction ordering (never-used first, then lastUsed, then oldest), detector scan correctness (mutable BlockPos reuse, canSeeSky/light-level API usage on 21.1.256, per-player loops), NBT null-safety on read (missing keys, malformed tags).\n2. **Concurrency/thread-safety**: everything must run on the server thread; check the tick handler and SavedData access patterns.\n3. **Performance**: detector scan cost per interval (cube radius 8 = ~4.6k positions/player — acceptable?); observation build allocations; pool eviction on every recordOutcome.\n4. **Design fidelity**: does anything contradict the design brief (e.g. pool entries containing non-action-space text, comfort tasks not being singletons, budget enforcement dropping SELF or ACTIONS)?\n5. **Test quality**: do the 8 new gametests actually assert the behaviors above, or are any tautological? Any test that could pass with the implementation broken?\n6. **Repo conventions**: init/ holder discipline, config gating, lang keys prefixed `siasworkshop.`, no stray comments.\n\n## Report format\n\nFor each finding: severity (blocking / should-fix / nit), file:line, one-paragraph explanation, suggested fix. End with an overall verdict: APPROVE / APPROVE-WITH-NITS / REQUEST-CHANGES. Be specific and skeptical — if you find nothing blocking, say so explicitly after checking the focus areas above.","subagent_type":"plan"}}}
