{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:55:24.051Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-decision-pool-goals--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Apply review fixes to agents slice","prompt":"Review of your agents slice came back REQUEST-CHANGES. A reviewer found 1 blocking bug + 6 should-fixes + a few nits. Apply the fixes below, keep everything else intact, re-run `./gradlew build` and `./gradlew runGameTestServer` (background + long timeout, they take minutes), and report. Do NOT commit; do NOT touch `mdocs/`.\n\n## Blocking\n\n1. **Shelter detector \"exposed\" check is dead code** — `content/agents/tasks/ComfortDetectors.java` (~line 110): `exposed` is computed as `level.getBrightness(LightLayer.SKY, center) >= 15`, but the detector only runs at night, when sky light at an exposed position is 4 (moonlight), not 15. So `exposed` is always false and the deficit degenerates to a bed check only. Fix: `boolean exposed = level.canSeeSky(center);`. Add a gametest phase to `shelterDeficitRaisesAndClearsAtNight` (new test method is fine too): night + bed within radius + NO cover → deficit must raise; then add cover → cleared.\n\n## Should-fix\n\n2. **Lease sweep pollutes the pool** — `TaskBoard.sweepLeases` records a FAILED pool anti-pattern for every lease expiry, but a timeout says nothing about whether the plan was bad. Fix: lease expiry must NOT write a pool entry (task still becomes FAILED with reason \"lease_expired\"). Adjust however you like (drop the pool params from sweepLeases, or have the production caller pass null) and simplify — this also moots the sweep duration metric concern.\n3. **Lease boundary** — `TaskBoard.java` steal branch (~line 87) and sweep (~line 138): expired should be `now >= leaseUntil`, not `now > leaseUntil` (claim at t with leaseTicks=100 → at t+100 the lease is spent). Update the BoardTask javadoc for `leaseUntilGameTime` to match, and add a boundary test (claim with leaseTicks=N, call at exactly createdAt+N → claimable by another claimant / swept).\n4. **Claimant verification** — `TaskBoard.complete` and `TaskBoard.fail` (~lines 99/115) resolve any CLAIMED task from any caller. Add a `UUID claimantUuid` parameter and require it to equal the task's claimant (return false otherwise). Update all callers and gametests.\n5. **NBT read robustness** — `AgentDecisionPool.read` (~line 186, `Outcome.valueOf`) and `TaskBoard.read` (~lines 225-226, `Type`/`Status` valueOf) throw on malformed entries, which can break world load. Wrap per-entry parsing in try/catch and skip unparseable entries, mirroring the existing schema_version skip.\n6. **Test gaps**:\n   - Add a `TaskBoard` NBT save/load round-trip test (UUID claimant path included).\n   - Add a lease-steal test: claim, advance time past lease, second claim by different UUID succeeds.\n   - Strengthen `observationFitsTokenBudget`: the current empty-world snapshot never exercises compression. Add a low-budget case (e.g. `AgentObservation.build(agent, 120)`) asserting SELF and AVAILABLE ACTIONS sections survive and middle sections compressed in the documented bottom-up order.\n\n## Nits (apply these too)\n\n7. `WorkshopAgentEntity.currentTask()` javadoc (~line 68) says \"until the shared task board lands\" — the board landed; reword to \"until a task-execution loop claims board tasks\".\n8. `TaskBoard.raiseIfAbsent` returns the existing task without refreshing `detail` — when the deficit persists, update the existing OPEN task's detail (copy-on-write like your other mutations) so e.g. dark-spot counts don't go stale.\n9. `AgentDecisionPool.recordSuccess(String, long now)` — `now` is unused; make it stamp `lastUsedGameTime` (that's clearly its intent) and setDirty.\n10. `TaskBoard` growth: DONE/FAILED history accumulates unbounded. Add a simple reap: keep at most 128 resolved (DONE+FAILED) tasks, dropping oldest resolved first; invoke it from the same periodic path as the lease sweep. No new config knob — a named constant is fine.\n\nDo NOT change: `Config.AGENTS_DEBUG_INSPECTOR` default, `AgentWorldData` naming, `findNearestFoundation` scan strategy (reviewer only noted it as future work).\n\n## Report back\n\n- Confirmation of each fix (file:line where relevant).\n- New gametest count and `./gradlew build` / `runGameTestServer` results.\n- Any signature changes to the public API surface you reported earlier, as an updated API list.","resume":"agent-0"}}}
