{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T05:13:20.395Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Review LLM slice diff","prompt":"You are a read-only code reviewer for a NeoForge 1.21.1 Minecraft mod at /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop (Java 21, package root com.siaws.siawsmod, mod id siasworkshop). Review the UNCOMMITTED diff for the \"agents v1: LLM client + build knowledge\" slice. Do NOT edit anything. Do NOT run gradle (the coordinator already has build + 25/25 gametests green).\n\n## Context\n\nThe slice adds: an OpenAI-compatible LLM client with template fallback (content/llm/), blueprint model + own .schem v2/v3 and vanilla-structure .nbt parsers + import folder (content/agents/build/), build-card datapack JSON loader, a /siasworkshop build command, an agent decision/execution loop claiming board tasks (content/agents/AgentDecisionLoop.java), and TaskBoard.release. Design sources: mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md (LLM decides/Java executes, constrained JSON, offline-first, never block server thread) and mdocs/wiki/reference/agent-embodiment-observation.md (action-space contract, retrieve-and-inject, grief guardrails, own parsers never copied from WorldEdit/Litematica). The pool/task-board APIs it builds on are in content/agents/pool/ and content/agents/tasks/ (already reviewed and committed earlier — only review their NEW modifications via git diff).\n\n## The diff\n\nNew files: content/llm/LlmClient.java, LlmPrompts.java, LlmActions.java; content/agents/build/{Blueprint,BlueprintLibrary,BlueprintParseException,SchemParser,StructureNbtParser,BuildCard,BuildCards,BuildQueue,BuildCommand}.java; content/agents/AgentDecisionLoop.java; gametest/AgentsLlmGameTest.java; resources/data/siasworkshop/structure/agentsllmgametest.empty.nbt; plus modifications to Config.java, SiasWorkshop.java, WorkshopAgentEntity.java, content/agents/tasks/{TaskBoard,ComfortDetectors}.java, gametest/AgentsGameTest.java, lang en_us.json, build.gradle, .gitignore. Use `git status` / `git diff` / read files in full.\n\n## Known history (do not re-report as findings)\n\n- The coordinator already fixed post-builder: execution/decision tick split (per-tick execution pass + interval-gated decisions), claim-key filter seam for tests, re-path throttling + no remote placement (navigate now side-effect-only; placement requires isCloseEnough), release-on-unplaceable + release-on-stuck, conditional chest withdraw, dedicated run-gametest dir + world wipe + seeded server config (agents.lightScanRadius=3), and the light gametest's enclosure/carpet/poll design. Review the CURRENT state of all of this.\n\n## Review focus (priority order)\n\n1. **LLM client thread-safety**: everything off-thread hops back via server.execute; no world mutation off-thread; executor lifecycle (static pools leaking?); in-flight request bookkeeping (inFlightRequests) cleanup on entity removal/server stop; HttpClient timeouts actually applied (connect vs request); failure paths never throw on the server thread.\n2. **Parser correctness**: Sponge v3 BlockData varint decoding (signedness, palette indexing bounds), v2 palette CompoundTag form, vanilla structure blocks[] indexing; gzip handling; malformed input → BlueprintParseException not crash; no unbounded allocations on hostile input (a 2GB Width?).\n3. **Safety boundaries**: LlmActions validation (can a model response cause block placement outside guardrails, item spawning, or non-action-space effects?); BuildCommand permission level; guardCheck coverage for every placement path (light + build); whitelist enforcement (build executor places blueprint palette only).\n4. **Loop state machine**: stuck/release/renew interactions — can a task deadlock (claim forever), double-resolve, or churn raise/release rapidly? lastPositions/stuckCycles static maps — leak agents over time?\n5. **SavedData/board additions**: release() semantics (claimant-verified? lease cleared? no pool write?).\n6. **Config**: all new knobs ranged, defaults sane, comments accurate.\n7. **Test quality**: do the 9 new tests in AgentsLlmGameTest assert real behavior? Any tautologies? The poll-based loop tests — racy leftovers?\n8. Conventions: lang keys prefixed, init/ holders, no stray comments, javadoc on public API.\n\n## Report\n\nPer finding: severity (blocking / should-fix / nit), file:line, explanation, suggested fix. Overall verdict: APPROVE / APPROVE-WITH-NITS / REQUEST-CHANGES. Be specific and skeptical; if nothing blocking, say so explicitly after checking each focus area.","subagent_type":"plan"}}}
