{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T06:36:28.937Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-009 | 2026-10-14 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live verification (user, runClient): Inspector snapshot-to-file works end-to-end (run/debug/siasworkshop/agent-observation-1792005907792.txt). Sparse night-village scene = 701 bytes ≈ 176 est tokens, well under the 900 budget (compression pass not even triggered; the earlier 1200-1500 sample was a much busier scene — trimming path itself is gametest-covered at low budget). Station-filtered actions confirmed (no deposit/withdraw without a chest). Nit: zero-count POIs (chest×0 crafting_table×0 furnace×0) waste ~35 tokens — suppress zeros in a future observation pass.`\n\n`SEQ-010 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge COMPLETE (26/26 gametests, build green, coordinator-rerun). LLM client (OpenAI-compatible, verified defaults http://localhost:1234/v1 + prism-ml/bonsai-27b; template fallback, bad_endpoint safe), own .schem v2/v3 + .nbt parsers (air skipped — real exports are mostly air; hostile-input hardened), build queue + /siasworkshop build cmd, build-card loader, AgentDecisionLoop (per-tick execution + interval decisions; release-on-stuck/unplaceable; pool citations), TaskBoard.release. War stories → setup/gametest-notes-1-21-1 (world persistence → dedicated run-gametest dir + wipe + seeded serverconfig; onEachTick fastutil trap; barrier frames as spawnable floors; production handlers race driven tests). Builder sub-agent timed out twice on the gametest debug loop — coordinator took over; lesson: give builders a strict \"report after N runs, don't spiral\" budget and keep the coordinator in the loop for integration-test debugging. All three agents-v1 initiatives now done. Next candidates (user picks): live LLM smoke test (enable llm.enabled against LM Studio), foundation-block GUI for pool/board inspection + blueprint queueing, chronicle/gossip flavor layer per local-llm-feasibility Phase 1, observation zero-POI nit.`\n\n<!-- Agents: append new entries below this line, in SEQ order. -->","oldString":"`SEQ-009 | 2026-10-14 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live verification (user, runClient): Inspector snapshot-to-file works end-to-end (run/debug/siasworkshop/agent-observation-1792005907792.txt). Sparse night-village scene = 701 bytes ≈ 176 est tokens, well under the 900 budget (compression pass not even triggered; the earlier 1200-1500 sample was a much busier scene — trimming path itself is gametest-covered at low budget). Station-filtered actions confirmed (no deposit/withdraw without a chest). Nit: zero-count POIs (chest×0 crafting_table×0 furnace×0) waste ~35 tokens — suppress zeros in a future observation pass.`\n\n<!-- Agents: append new entries below this line, in SEQ order. -->","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
