{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T17:52:42.717Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"- **LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only (IPv4), and `localhost` is unsafe in modded\n  JVMs.** Dev launchers (ModDevGradle runClient, CurseForge) set\n  `-Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system`; with it, `localhost` resolves to ::1\n  first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of\n  falling back to IPv4 (reproduced standalone with the same flag; without the\n  flag it silently works). The endpoint default is therefore `127.0.0.1`.","oldString":"- **LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only (IPv4)**; `localhost` may resolve to ::1\n  first. The endpoint default uses localhost and worked on this machine, but if\n  a setup ever fails to connect at all, `127.0.0.1` is the first thing to try.","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T17:52:42.712Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"- **LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only (IPv4), and `localhost` is unsafe in modded\n  JVMs.** Dev launchers (ModDevGradle runClient, CurseForge) set\n  `-Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system`; with it, `localhost` resolves to ::1\n  first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of\n  falling back to IPv4 (reproduced standalone with the same flag; without the\n  flag it silently works). The endpoint default is therefore `127.0.0.1`.","oldString":"- **LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only (IPv4)**; `localhost` may resolve to ::1\n  first. The endpoint default uses localhost and worked on this machine, but if\n  a setup ever fails to connect at all, `127.0.0.1` is the first thing to try.","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md"}}}
