{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:48:44.899Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"<!-- Agents: append new entries below this line, in SEQ order. -->\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio. T1 (light task via template fallback) and T2 (build queue) passed earlier in the day. T3 (LLM decision path) exposed four real bugs, all fixed and committed: (1) LM Studio (llama.cpp) rejects response_format \"json_object\" (HTTP 400; only json_schema/text allowed), surfacing client-side as ClosedChannelException — field dropped, system prompt constrains JSON instead (f974a47); (2) dev launchers set -Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system, so localhost resolves ::1-first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of falling back to IPv4, while LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only — endpoint default now 127.0.0.1; reproduced standalone with the same flag (c9ebf8d); (3) reasoning models burn the whole maxTokens budget on hidden thinking (bonsai-27b: 511/511 completion tokens reasoning, empty content, finish_reason=length) — maxTokens default 512->1024, range 16~2048, timeoutSeconds default 30->120, bad_json WARN now includes a 200-char preview of the raw reply (212f147); (4) parseJsonObject required a leading '{' while bonsai answers in json code fences — parser now extracts the first {...} span. Observability added: INFO on LLM decisions + task claims, WARN with reason on fallback, /siasworkshop board debug command. HARD-WON TRAPS: (a) quit-to-menu != client restart — classes and ModConfigSpec bake at JVM start; re-entering the world keeps old code/spec (cost us one full test round); (b) config values outside the RUNNING spec's range are silently \"corrected\" at load — hand-edits beyond the running max get reverted, always re-read the file after load; (c) a commit once claimed a change it didn't contain — verified via javap on build/classes constants; do that when config behaves impossibly. T3 verdict: \"decided via LLM: light {}\" logged twice (13:43:54, 13:44:21) even on the stale 512 spec — intermittent, since reasoning sometimes exceeds 512 (bad_json with empty preview). Reliability needs one true client restart with the 212f147 classes. Model notes: bonsai-27b reasons ~450-900 tokens per decision (60-120s on a loaded M3 Pro); a smaller non-reasoning model is the likely production choice for snappy decisions (config-only switch of llm.model). One isolated http_400 from LM Studio mid-session, unrepeated. Wire-compat writeup: reference/local-llm-feasibility.`","oldString":"<!-- Agents: append new entries below this line, in SEQ order. -->","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:48:44.905Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## How to resume\n\n1. Read `AGENTS.md`, this file, `setup/agent-shared-ledger` (latest SEQ entries —\n   SEQ-011 holds the full live-LLM-test story), and\n   `reference/agent-embodiment-observation` (design source of truth).\n2. `mdocs status` — idle/COMPLETE.\n3. LLM live smoke test PASSED 2026-10-15 (SEQ-011). Fixes in f974a47, c9ebf8d,\n   212f147; 27/27 gametests green; wire-compat notes in\n   reference/local-llm-feasibility.\n4. Next candidates (user picks): foundation-block GUI for pool/board + blueprint\n   queueing; chronicle/gossip flavor layer (local-llm-feasibility Phase 1);\n   shelter-task execution; observation zero-POI nit; applyDecisionAction mapping\n   for valid-but-idle actions like light(); production model choice (fast\n   non-reasoning local model) + decision-latency tuning.","oldString":"## How to resume\n\n1. Read `AGENTS.md`, this file, `setup/agent-shared-ledger` (latest SEQ entries),\n   and `reference/agent-embodiment-observation` (design source of truth).\n2. `mdocs status` / read `mdocs/.workflow-state.json` — should be idle/COMPLETE.\n3. Confirm with user: commit the spike diff? close `publish-curseforge-1-0-2`?\n4. Activate `agents-v1-decision-pool-goals--2026-10-14`\n   (`mdocs resume` → steps UNDERSTAND…EXECUTE), including the SEQ-007 scope\n   additions (compression + verbatim debug file). Optionally verify the LM Studio\n   endpoint with curl first (above).","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/session-recovery-2026-10-14.md"}}}
