{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:57:10.374Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"- **Cloud providers need an API key.** `llm.apiKey` (default empty) is sent as an\n  `Authorization: Bearer` header when non-blank; empty means no header, which is\n  what local endpoints (LM Studio, Ollama) expect. To switch to a cloud model,\n  only the config changes: `endpoint`, `model`, `apiKey`.\n- **Failures must be visible in latest.log at INFO/WARN, not DEBUG.**","oldString":"- **Failures must be visible in latest.log at INFO/WARN, not DEBUG.**","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:57:10.378Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"- **Cloud providers need an API key.** `llm.apiKey` (default empty) is sent as an\n  `Authorization: Bearer` header when non-blank; empty means no header, which is\n  what local endpoints (LM Studio, Ollama) expect. To switch to a cloud model,\n  only the config changes: `endpoint`, `model`, `apiKey`.\n- **Failures must be visible in latest.log at INFO/WARN, not DEBUG.**","oldString":"- **Failures must be visible in latest.log at INFO/WARN, not DEBUG.**","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:57:26.256Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"git add -A src/ mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md && git commit -m \"feat(agents): decision-shaped prompt + cloud API key support\n\nThe live run exposed why model choices looked wrong: the prompt never\nlisted the open tasks at all — the model could only guess from the\ncapability list and picked things like light() that the decision layer\ntreats as 'valid but not decision-shaped' and falls back.\n\n- userPrompt now renders OPEN TASKS with their exact claim keys and a\n  DECISION block limited to the three actions the v1 loop honors\n  (claim/rest/say), explaining that hands run automatically after a\n  claim; the raw 15-action dump is gone from the decision prompt.\n- Observation's [AVAILABLE ACTIONS] renamed to\n  [CAPABILITIES once working a task] so the prompt tells one coherent\n  story (capabilities are what the executor does, not a menu).\n- llm.apiKey config (default empty): sent as Authorization Bearer when\n  set, no header when empty — same client now works against cloud\n  OpenAI-compatible endpoints by config change alone.\n- llmPromptListsOpenTaskKeys gametest pins the prompt contract (28/28).\" && git log --oneline -1"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T19:57:26.260Z","type":"tool","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"git add -A src/ mdocs/wiki/reference/local-llm-feasibility.md && git commit -m \"feat(agents): decision-shaped prompt + cloud API key support\n\nThe live run exposed why model choices looked wrong: the prompt never\nlisted the open tasks at all — the model could only guess from the\ncapability list and picked things like light() that the decision layer\ntreats as 'valid but not decision-shaped' and falls back.\n\n- userPrompt now renders OPEN TASKS with their exact claim keys and a\n  DECISION block limited to the three actions the v1 loop honors\n  (claim/rest/say), explaining that hands run automatically after a\n  claim; the raw 15-action dump is gone from the decision prompt.\n- Observation's [AVAILABLE ACTIONS] renamed to\n  [CAPABILITIES once working a task] so the prompt tells one coherent\n  story (capabilities are what the executor does, not a menu).\n- llm.apiKey config (default empty): sent as Authorization Bearer when\n  set, no header when empty — same client now works against cloud\n  OpenAI-compatible endpoints by config change alone.\n- llmPromptListsOpenTaskKeys gametest pins the prompt contract (28/28).\" && git log --oneline -1"}}}
