{"timestamp":"2026-10-16T21:22:02.810Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-019 | 2026-10-16 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Pattern-tree descriptor design done, parked in wiki reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design (initiative plan item checked off). Core decisions: mod = MCP SERVER owning the tool registry; sidecar = MCP client + model host; transport = sidecar subprocess with MCP over child stdio (sidecar in client role on its own pipes — no ports, lifecycle bound to server; loopback HTTP rejected as escape-hatch only). Four tool kinds (observe / category / pattern / effect); expansion via PATTERN CARDS riding in tool results ({result, children}) — retrieve-and-inject falls out, no tools/list_changed dependency, mod prunes children situationally. Session-state split: conversation in sidecar, world truth in mod, task board stays underneath (long horizon + multi-agent); convergence via observe.task polling. Safety: effect schema validation stays in-mod (LlmActions successor), guardrails unchanged, structured rejects. Variance: profiles in sidecar, prompt-constrained JSON first-class (local-llm-feasibility: locals do constrained schemas fine, open function calling poorly). Flag agents.mcp.enabled default-OFF; template fallback only when the MCP PATH is down. Reference walk = the building workflow, every hop mapped onto existing v1 machinery (BuildCards/BlueprintLibrary/BuildQueue/executors). Next: spike S0 — plumbing + parity (3 v1 decision tools, one local + one cloud model; latency + malformed rate vs v1).`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
