{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T03:40:52.928Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## Summary\n\n`mdocs command initiative.update --json '{\"id\": ..., \"updates\": {...}, \"progressNote\": \"...\"}'` on a flat-file initiative **rewrites the entire markdown file from the parsed model**, silently discarding every section that is not Objective/Plan/Progress Log/Artifacts, truncating multi-line list entries to their first line, and renaming the file as a side effect.\n\nObserved on harness-mdocs 2.1.0 (build gitSha `231a9a6`).\n\n## Repro\n\nInitiative file with a rich body (Direction / Motivation / Research questions / Considered-and-set-aside sections, multi-line wrapped Progress Log entries, Plan checkboxes), then:\n\n```bash\nmdocs command initiative.update --json '{\"id\":\"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15\",\"updates\":{\"status\":\"active\",\"owner\":\"coordinator\"},\"progressNote\":\"[2026-10-16] Resumed per handoff ...\"}'\n```\n\n## Observed\n\n- All body sections except Objective/Plan/Progress Log are **gone** after the call.\n- Progress Log entries are **truncated to their first line** (continuation lines lost).\n- The file is **renamed** (`formatFileName`): `mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15.md` → `mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md`, showing up in git as delete+add.\n\n## Root cause (dist, 2.1.0)\n\n`dist/core/managers/initiative.js` `update()` — flat-file branch (~line 279):\n\n1. Parses the file into the model (objective / plan / progressLog / artifacts).\n2. Re-renders the whole file from that model only (~lines 300–306):\n\n   ```js\n   const content = this.toFrontmatter(initiative) +\n       `## Objective\\n${initiative.objective}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Plan\\n${initiative.plan.map(p => formatPlanItem(p)).join('\\n')}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Progress Log\\n${initiative.progressLog.map(l => `- ${l}`).join('\\n')}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Artifacts\\n${initiative.artifacts.map(a => `- ${a}`).join('\\n')}`;\n   fs.writeFileSync(newPath, content, 'utf8');\n   ```\n\n   Any section not in the model is dropped; `newPath` comes from `formatFileName(initiative)` (the rename side effect).\n3. `parseListSection` (~line 47) keeps only lines starting with `- `, so wrapped multi-line entries lose everything after line 1. Same for `parsePlanItem` descriptions.\n\n**Inconsistent with directory mode**: the directory branch routes through `store.update()` → `initiative-store.js` `updateStatusFile()`, which is surgical (front-matter line rewrite + `appendProgressNote` in place, and even has a body-preserving `metadata-only` contract mode). Flat-file mode has no equivalent preservation path.\n\n## Suggested directions\n\n- Make flat-mode `update()` surgical like `updateStatusFile`: rewrite only touched front-matter keys in place and append the progress note; never regenerate the body.\n- If a full re-render is ever desired, preserve unknown sections verbatim (split body into known/unknown, re-render known, re-append unknown) and fold continuation lines into list items in `parseListSection`.\n- Don't rename on update, or gate it behind an explicit flag — silent delete+add wrecks git history.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny consumer keeping durable context in initiative bodies (direction decisions, motivation, research questions — exactly what initiatives are for in long-running projects) loses it on the first `initiative.update`. I hit this in a live session and had to restore the file by hand from session context. A parse→render roundtrip that is not lossless should never be the default write path.\n\nWorkaround until fixed: hand-edit initiative files + `mdocs validate`; avoid `initiative.update` on files with rich bodies.\n","path":".tmp/mdocs-issue-initiative-update.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T03:40:52.932Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## Summary\n\n`mdocs command initiative.update --json '{\"id\": ..., \"updates\": {...}, \"progressNote\": \"...\"}'` on a flat-file initiative **rewrites the entire markdown file from the parsed model**, silently discarding every section that is not Objective/Plan/Progress Log/Artifacts, truncating multi-line list entries to their first line, and renaming the file as a side effect.\n\nObserved on harness-mdocs 2.1.0 (build gitSha `231a9a6`).\n\n## Repro\n\nInitiative file with a rich body (Direction / Motivation / Research questions / Considered-and-set-aside sections, multi-line wrapped Progress Log entries, Plan checkboxes), then:\n\n```bash\nmdocs command initiative.update --json '{\"id\":\"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15\",\"updates\":{\"status\":\"active\",\"owner\":\"coordinator\"},\"progressNote\":\"[2026-10-16] Resumed per handoff ...\"}'\n```\n\n## Observed\n\n- All body sections except Objective/Plan/Progress Log are **gone** after the call.\n- Progress Log entries are **truncated to their first line** (continuation lines lost).\n- The file is **renamed** (`formatFileName`): `mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15.md` → `mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md`, showing up in git as delete+add.\n\n## Root cause (dist, 2.1.0)\n\n`dist/core/managers/initiative.js` `update()` — flat-file branch (~line 279):\n\n1. Parses the file into the model (objective / plan / progressLog / artifacts).\n2. Re-renders the whole file from that model only (~lines 300–306):\n\n   ```js\n   const content = this.toFrontmatter(initiative) +\n       `## Objective\\n${initiative.objective}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Plan\\n${initiative.plan.map(p => formatPlanItem(p)).join('\\n')}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Progress Log\\n${initiative.progressLog.map(l => `- ${l}`).join('\\n')}\\n\\n` +\n       `## Artifacts\\n${initiative.artifacts.map(a => `- ${a}`).join('\\n')}`;\n   fs.writeFileSync(newPath, content, 'utf8');\n   ```\n\n   Any section not in the model is dropped; `newPath` comes from `formatFileName(initiative)` (the rename side effect).\n3. `parseListSection` (~line 47) keeps only lines starting with `- `, so wrapped multi-line entries lose everything after line 1. Same for `parsePlanItem` descriptions.\n\n**Inconsistent with directory mode**: the directory branch routes through `store.update()` → `initiative-store.js` `updateStatusFile()`, which is surgical (front-matter line rewrite + `appendProgressNote` in place, and even has a body-preserving `metadata-only` contract mode). Flat-file mode has no equivalent preservation path.\n\n## Suggested directions\n\n- Make flat-mode `update()` surgical like `updateStatusFile`: rewrite only touched front-matter keys in place and append the progress note; never regenerate the body.\n- If a full re-render is ever desired, preserve unknown sections verbatim (split body into known/unknown, re-render known, re-append unknown) and fold continuation lines into list items in `parseListSection`.\n- Don't rename on update, or gate it behind an explicit flag — silent delete+add wrecks git history.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny consumer keeping durable context in initiative bodies (direction decisions, motivation, research questions — exactly what initiatives are for in long-running projects) loses it on the first `initiative.update`. I hit this in a live session and had to restore the file by hand from session context. A parse→render roundtrip that is not lossless should never be the default write path.\n\nWorkaround until fixed: hand-edit initiative files + `mdocs validate`; avoid `initiative.update` on files with rich bodies.\n","path":".tmp/mdocs-issue-initiative-update.md"}}}
