{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:56:10.872Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-022 | 2026-10-16 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S1 done — the MCP path is REAL in the mod. Config agents.mcp.* block (enabled default OFF — no Python for CurseForge installs; command default \"python3 sidecar/sidecar.py\" resolved against the game cwd, abs path recommended; decisionTimeoutSeconds 180). content/mcp/McpSidecar: spawn/lifecycle on server start/stop, symmetric newline-JSON-RPC over child stdio with BOTH peers acting client+server on the same pipes (sidecar initiates initialize on its stdout; mod calls the sidecar's decide tool on its stdin — the D2 symmetric-pipe extension), reader thread + pending-future map, inbound mod-tool calls queued to the server thread with the reader parked (server thread never blocks on the sidecar — decisions are async end-to-end like LlmClient.request, so NO duplex deadlock), every failure collapses to CallResult(usable/failure) → template fallback. content/mcp/McpTools: the mod's S0 catalog (observe_self/observe_board/claim/rest/say, agent passed as uuid arg, tools stateless) with structured {\"reject\":...} validation. AgentDecisionLoop routes via sidecar ahead of the direct llm.* path (MCP takes precedence when enabled+alive) and reconciles results (reported claim the board doesn't reflect → template claim). PYTHON: real sidecar.py bridge (client role: initialize → serve decide(agent) → pull observation/board via mod tools → model prompt/native surface → validate → execute claim/rest/say via mod tools → summary) + test_sidecar_bridge.py (sidecar.py vs mockmod.py over crossed pipes = production topology, PASS; mock S0 schemas grew an optional agent arg to match the Java surface). GAMETESTS AgentsMcpGameTest ×4 (34/34 green): handshake+catalog serving, full decide cycle claiming on the REAL board via the fake peer (in-JVM PipedStreams), malformed-call rejects (say w/o msg, unknown tool, observe w/o agent), dead-sidecar template fallback via the loop's own handleMcpResult. Gametest traps cost one round each: (1) @GameTest has no timeout attribute in these mappings — plain template only; (2) the PRODUCTION tick loop runs during tests and immediately fails an intentionally-malformed test build task — assert the board RECORD + claimantUuid, not live claim state; (3) shared batch world: the peer must claim its OWN key, never open.get(0) (a previous test's leftover task led the claim astray); (4) the production loop can template-claim open tasks for a test's idle agent — don't assert \"nothing claimed\" board state for probe tests. Live in-game verification (runClient + agents.mcp.enabled=true with a real model command) still pending — user-side, like the SEQ-011 rounds. Remaining initiative items: scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:56:10.878Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-022 | 2026-10-16 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S1 done — the MCP path is REAL in the mod. Config agents.mcp.* block (enabled default OFF — no Python for CurseForge installs; command default \"python3 sidecar/sidecar.py\" resolved against the game cwd, abs path recommended; decisionTimeoutSeconds 180). content/mcp/McpSidecar: spawn/lifecycle on server start/stop, symmetric newline-JSON-RPC over child stdio with BOTH peers acting client+server on the same pipes (sidecar initiates initialize on its stdout; mod calls the sidecar's decide tool on its stdin — the D2 symmetric-pipe extension), reader thread + pending-future map, inbound mod-tool calls queued to the server thread with the reader parked (server thread never blocks on the sidecar — decisions are async end-to-end like LlmClient.request, so NO duplex deadlock), every failure collapses to CallResult(usable/failure) → template fallback. content/mcp/McpTools: the mod's S0 catalog (observe_self/observe_board/claim/rest/say, agent passed as uuid arg, tools stateless) with structured {\"reject\":...} validation. AgentDecisionLoop routes via sidecar ahead of the direct llm.* path (MCP takes precedence when enabled+alive) and reconciles results (reported claim the board doesn't reflect → template claim). PYTHON: real sidecar.py bridge (client role: initialize → serve decide(agent) → pull observation/board via mod tools → model prompt/native surface → validate → execute claim/rest/say via mod tools → summary) + test_sidecar_bridge.py (sidecar.py vs mockmod.py over crossed pipes = production topology, PASS; mock S0 schemas grew an optional agent arg to match the Java surface). GAMETESTS AgentsMcpGameTest ×4 (34/34 green): handshake+catalog serving, full decide cycle claiming on the REAL board via the fake peer (in-JVM PipedStreams), malformed-call rejects (say w/o msg, unknown tool, observe w/o agent), dead-sidecar template fallback via the loop's own handleMcpResult. Gametest traps cost one round each: (1) @GameTest has no timeout attribute in these mappings — plain template only; (2) the PRODUCTION tick loop runs during tests and immediately fails an intentionally-malformed test build task — assert the board RECORD + claimantUuid, not live claim state; (3) shared batch world: the peer must claim its OWN key, never open.get(0) (a previous test's leftover task led the claim astray); (4) the production loop can template-claim open tasks for a test's idle agent — don't assert \"nothing claimed\" board state for probe tests. Live in-game verification (runClient + agents.mcp.enabled=true with a real model command) still pending — user-side, like the SEQ-011 rounds. Remaining initiative items: scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:56:24.445Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## S1 in-mod results (2026-10-16)\n\nThe MCP path is real in the mod (ledger SEQ-022): `Config agents.mcp.*` (default OFF),\n`content/mcp/McpSidecar` (spawn/lifecycle, symmetric JSON-RPC over child stdio, both\npeers client+server, failure collapse + template fallback), `content/mcp/McpTools` (S0\ncatalog, server-thread dispatch, structured rejects), decision routing with the sidecar\ntaking precedence over the direct `llm.*` path. The Python `sidecar.py` bridge serves\n`decide(agent)` and runs the observe → model → claim/rest/say loop through mod tools.\n\n- 34/34 gametests green, including 4 MCP tests against an in-JVM fake peer\n  (handshake/catalog, decide-claims-on-the-real-board, malformed rejects, dead-sidecar\n  fallback) and the python bridge test over crossed pipes (production topology).\n- One design refinement landed during S1: because the mod's `decide` call is async and\n  inbound mod-tool calls are server-thread-queued, the duplex flow cannot deadlock — the\n  constraint that shaped the whole transport design.\n- Live in-game verification (runClient + enabled flag + real model) is the remaining\n  user-side step, same pattern as the SEQ-011 live rounds.\n\n## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","oldString":"## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:56:24.451Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## S1 in-mod results (2026-10-16)\n\nThe MCP path is real in the mod (ledger SEQ-022): `Config agents.mcp.*` (default OFF),\n`content/mcp/McpSidecar` (spawn/lifecycle, symmetric JSON-RPC over child stdio, both\npeers client+server, failure collapse + template fallback), `content/mcp/McpTools` (S0\ncatalog, server-thread dispatch, structured rejects), decision routing with the sidecar\ntaking precedence over the direct `llm.*` path. The Python `sidecar.py` bridge serves\n`decide(agent)` and runs the observe → model → claim/rest/say loop through mod tools.\n\n- 34/34 gametests green, including 4 MCP tests against an in-JVM fake peer\n  (handshake/catalog, decide-claims-on-the-real-board, malformed rejects, dead-sidecar\n  fallback) and the python bridge test over crossed pipes (production topology).\n- One design refinement landed during S1: because the mod's `decide` call is async and\n  inbound mod-tool calls are server-thread-queued, the duplex flow cannot deadlock — the\n  constraint that shaped the whole transport design.\n- Live in-game verification (runClient + enabled flag + real model) is the remaining\n  user-side step, same pattern as the SEQ-011 live rounds.\n\n## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","oldString":"## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:56:38.485Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"./node_modules/.bin/mdocs validate --summary 2>&1 | head -3 && git add -A && git commit -m \"feat(agents): S1 — in-mod MCP sidecar path behind default-OFF flag\n\nConfig agents.mcp.* block (enabled default OFF — no Python for CurseForge\ninstalls; command; decision timeout). content/mcp/McpSidecar: spawn/lifecycle on\nserver start/stop, symmetric newline-JSON-RPC over child stdio with both peers\nacting client+server (the D2 extension), reader thread + pending futures, inbound\nmod-tool calls server-thread-queued (server never blocks on the sidecar — async\nend-to-end, no duplex deadlock), failure collapse to CallResult. content/mcp/\nMcpTools: the mod's S0 catalog with structured rejects. AgentDecisionLoop routes\nvia the sidecar ahead of the direct llm.* path with template fallback.\n\nPython: real sidecar.py bridge (serves decide(agent), runs observe -> model ->\nclaim/rest/say through mod tools, --replay offline mode) + bridge test over\ncrossed pipes (production topology, PASS).\n\nGametests (34/34 green): handshake+catalog, decide claims on the real board via\nan in-JVM fake peer, malformed-call rejects, dead-sidecar fallback. mdocs:\nledger SEQ-022, initiative S1 tick, design doc S1 section.\" 2>&1 | tail -2 && git log --oneline -2 && git status --short | wc -l"}}}
