{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:13:56.370Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-023 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESUMED-FIX | S1 gate-order bug fix. The MCP branch in AgentDecisionLoop.decide() sat BELOW the !llm.enabled early-return, so agents.mcp.enabled=true alone never activated the sidecar path — the user's first live config (llm.enabled=false + mcp.enabled=true) silently template-claimed instead. Fix: MCP routing moved ahead of the llm gate; the gate order extracted into pure route(mcpEnabled, sidecarAvailable, llmEnabled) → DecisionRoute{MCP,DIRECT_LLM,TEMPLATE}, public for gametests (ModConfigSpec bakes at JVM start, so precedence is pinned by testing the pure fn): mcp-alive beats everything; dead/off sidecar falls to DIRECT when llm.enabled else TEMPLATE. Gametest mcpGateOrderPrecedence (6 assertions, 35 total). Config comments clarified: the sidecar child inherits the GAME dir as cwd (run/ in dev) so relative paths miss — absolute is the reliable choice (user's command was relative); 'fall back to templates' corrected to direct-path-or-templates. Live-test recipe: absolute command python3 /Users/.../sidecar/sidecar.py (endpoint/model defaults already target LM Studio bonsai-27b), llm.enabled can stay OFF — it is now genuinely orthogonal to the MCP path. Next: user live-runs S1; then scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:13:56.376Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-023 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESUMED-FIX | S1 gate-order bug fix. The MCP branch in AgentDecisionLoop.decide() sat BELOW the !llm.enabled early-return, so agents.mcp.enabled=true alone never activated the sidecar path — the user's first live config (llm.enabled=false + mcp.enabled=true) silently template-claimed instead. Fix: MCP routing moved ahead of the llm gate; the gate order extracted into pure route(mcpEnabled, sidecarAvailable, llmEnabled) → DecisionRoute{MCP,DIRECT_LLM,TEMPLATE}, public for gametests (ModConfigSpec bakes at JVM start, so precedence is pinned by testing the pure fn): mcp-alive beats everything; dead/off sidecar falls to DIRECT when llm.enabled else TEMPLATE. Gametest mcpGateOrderPrecedence (6 assertions, 35 total). Config comments clarified: the sidecar child inherits the GAME dir as cwd (run/ in dev) so relative paths miss — absolute is the reliable choice (user's command was relative); 'fall back to templates' corrected to direct-path-or-templates. Live-test recipe: absolute command python3 /Users/.../sidecar/sidecar.py (endpoint/model defaults already target LM Studio bonsai-27b), llm.enabled can stay OFF — it is now genuinely orthogonal to the MCP path. Next: user live-runs S1; then scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
