{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:14:44.512Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"fix(agents): route MCP decisions ahead of the llm.enabled gate\n\nThe MCP branch in AgentDecisionLoop.decide() sat below the\n!llm.enabled early-return, so agents.mcp.enabled=true alone silently\ntemplate-claimed instead of using the sidecar — the config comment's\n\"takes precedence over the direct llm.* path\" was not what the code did.\n\nThe gate order is now route(mcpEnabled, sidecarAvailable, llmEnabled)\n-> DecisionRoute{MCP, DIRECT_LLM, TEMPLATE}: a live sidecar wins over\neverything (no llm.* involvement), a dead or flag-off sidecar falls to\nthe direct path when llm.enabled, else templates. Pure + public so the\nmcpGateOrderPrecedence gametest pins the precedence without toggling\nModConfigSpec values (they bake at JVM start).\n\nAlso clarify the agents.mcp.command comment: the sidecar child\ninherits the game directory as its working directory (run/ in dev),\nso relative paths miss and an absolute path is the reliable choice.\n\n35/35 gametests green (SEQ-023).\n","path":".tmp/commit-msg.txt"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:14:44.520Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"fix(agents): route MCP decisions ahead of the llm.enabled gate\n\nThe MCP branch in AgentDecisionLoop.decide() sat below the\n!llm.enabled early-return, so agents.mcp.enabled=true alone silently\ntemplate-claimed instead of using the sidecar — the config comment's\n\"takes precedence over the direct llm.* path\" was not what the code did.\n\nThe gate order is now route(mcpEnabled, sidecarAvailable, llmEnabled)\n-> DecisionRoute{MCP, DIRECT_LLM, TEMPLATE}: a live sidecar wins over\neverything (no llm.* involvement), a dead or flag-off sidecar falls to\nthe direct path when llm.enabled, else templates. Pure + public so the\nmcpGateOrderPrecedence gametest pins the precedence without toggling\nModConfigSpec values (they bake at JVM start).\n\nAlso clarify the agents.mcp.command comment: the sidecar child\ninherits the game directory as its working directory (run/ in dev),\nso relative paths miss and an absolute path is the reliable choice.\n\n35/35 gametests green (SEQ-023).\n","path":".tmp/commit-msg.txt"}}}
