{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T07:29:35.937Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Live-test recipe: absolute command python3 /Users/.../sidecar/sidecar.py (endpoint/model defaults already target LM Studio bonsai-27b), llm.enabled can stay OFF — it is now genuinely orthogonal to the MCP path. Next: user live-runs S1; then scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-024 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | LIVE S1 TEST in TestSidecar01 PASSED + 4 real bugs found and fixed. Setup catch first: serverconfig is PER-WORLD — the user's agents.mcp.enabled edit lived in TestLLM_01, the new world TestSidecar01 got defaults (mcp silently off); fixed by copying the toml into the world's serverconfig AND into run/defaultconfigs/ (seeds every future world). Config override confirmed via \"Found config file override\" log line. RUN: sidecar.py spawned at server start (pid in new INFO line), destroyed cleanly on stop; 13 decisions over ~18 min, ALL via MCP, zero transport failures; LM Studio showed matching inbound traffic. Model behavior: bonsai latched onto the first-listed open task (build:mazons:-20,86,0) and re-picked it every lap. FOUND+FIXED (commit follows): (1) COMFORT_SHELTER leaked into observe_board/claim — the exclusion lived only in decide()'s private chain while openTasks()' javadoc claimed it (the live run caught the model claiming shelter, executor instantly releasing, template fallback claiming light — ping-pong exactly as v1 feared); fixed by moving the exclusion INTO openTasks() (single source: decide/MCP surface/fallback), pinned by gametest mcpShelterHiddenFromSurface (mock player owns the shelter key so only the exclusion can hide it). (2) sidecar reject payloads surfaced as decision \"unknown\" with empty detail → now WARN+fallback with the reject reason; {\"decision\":\"error\"} also collapses to WARN+fallback (was a silent no-op cycle). (3) STUCK_CYCLES 4→40 — 4 ticks is 0.2s of no movement, brutal under the observed dev lag (\"Can't keep up\" 10-21s constantly with bonsai on the same machine); unroutable anchor y=86 caused claim→stuck-release→re-claim spin burning a bonsai call per lap. (4) release cooldown RELEASE_COOLDOWN_TICKS=5min per agent per task key: decide() filters recently-released keys so the model can't re-pick a task the executor just gave up on (also breaks the spin when the anchor stays unroutable). Plus McpSidecar INFO \"sidecar started (pid N)\" on successful spawn (was warn-only). Gametests 35→36. NOT fixed (design, later initiative): model task-choice diversity (first-listed latch), observation ordering, LM Studio-side latency. The user's flat-ground task went unclaimed all session — retest with the cooldown should let the agent move past the unroutable anchor to reachable work.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"Live-test recipe: absolute command python3 /Users/.../sidecar/sidecar.py (endpoint/model defaults already target LM Studio bonsai-27b), llm.enabled can stay OFF — it is now genuinely orthogonal to the MCP path. Next: user live-runs S1; then scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
