_CYCLES 4→40 — 4 ticks is 0.2s of no movement, brutal under the observed dev lag (\"Can't keep up\" 10-21s constantly with bonsai on the same machine); unroutable anchor y=86 caused claim→stuck-release→re-claim spin burning a bonsai call per lap. (4) release cooldown RELEASE_COOLDOWN_TICKS=5min per agent per task key: decide() filters recently-released keys so the model can't re-pick a task the executor just gave up on (also breaks the spin when the anchor stays unroutable). Plus McpSidecar INFO \"sidecar started (pid N)\" on successful spawn (was warn-only). Gametests 35→36. NOT fixed (design, later initiative): model task-choice diversity (first-listed latch), observation ordering, LM Studio-side latency. The user's flat-ground task went unclaimed all session — retest with the cooldown should let the agent move past the unroutable anchor to reachable work.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"Live-test recipe: absolute command python3 /Users/.../sidecar/sidecar.py (endpoint/model defaults already target LM Studio bonsai-27b), llm.enabled can stay OFF — it is now genuinely orthogonal to the MCP path. Next: user live-runs S1; then scenario corpus (Q4) + migration recommendation.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
