{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T08:12:27.105Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Status: proposed, awaits user go-ahead after the S1-fix retest round.`\n\n`SEQ-026 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S1 RETEST PASSED — the MCP path is LIVE-VERIFIED end-to-end in TestSidecar01. Sequence: 02:10:51 user re-raised build:mazons:-19,81,-6 (the earlier FAILED task is terminal; raiseIfAbsent mints a fresh same-key task) after putting STONE BRICKS in a chest within stationRadius of the anchor; 02:11:14 the model claimed it (23s lap — fastest of the session); the agent walked, withdrew, placed, and the build WORKED (\"ok it worked\", user eyewitness). Full session evidence: (1) the cooldown march — after each release the model picked a DIFFERENT task (-20,86,0 → -18,81,-2 → -15,81,-2 → -19,81,-6), zero re-latching; (2) the three y=81 pre-fix-era laps FAILED with missing_material:minecraft:stone_bricks — the mazons palette wants stone BRICKS, the user's chests had plain stone, and the fetch searches within 16 blocks of the ANCHOR (agents.stationRadius default), not of the player — arrival itself worked every time (placement loop only runs within 2 blocks of anchor); (3) comfort:light claimed 01:59:00 completed and vanished from the board — the first full MCP decide→claim→walk→place→auto-complete cycle; (4) -20,86,0 reclaimed at 02:08:16 after its cooldown expired and released again — the standing cooldown loop for a persistently unroutable anchor works as designed (one lap per 5min window). KNOWN EXECUTOR WARTS for a future polish pass: withdrawOnce visits only the FIRST chest in scan order per cycle (a stocked chest behind an unstocked one is invisible); arrival circling when the navigator can't close the last 2 blocks to an anchor (stuck detector only counts UNMOVING ticks — a circling agent moves and evades it; these laps happened to freeze during lag bursts, but a no-progress watchdog is the real fix); board dump shows COMFORT_SHELTER OPEN but the MCP surface hides it (post-SEQ-024 fix confirmed in vivo). Vindication verdict: when walkability + materials line up, the entire S1 chain closes. Next: hot-plug debug access (SEQ-025) would have turned this whole forensics session into a live tap; scenario corpus (Q4) gains its first real-world failure classes: unroutable anchor, missing/wrong material, station-radius ignorance.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"Status: proposed, awaits user go-ahead after the S1-fix retest round.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T08:12:27.111Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Status: proposed, awaits user go-ahead after the S1-fix retest round.`\n\n`SEQ-026 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S1 RETEST PASSED — the MCP path is LIVE-VERIFIED end-to-end in TestSidecar01. Sequence: 02:10:51 user re-raised build:mazons:-19,81,-6 (the earlier FAILED task is terminal; raiseIfAbsent mints a fresh same-key task) after putting STONE BRICKS in a chest within stationRadius of the anchor; 02:11:14 the model claimed it (23s lap — fastest of the session); the agent walked, withdrew, placed, and the build WORKED (\"ok it worked\", user eyewitness). Full session evidence: (1) the cooldown march — after each release the model picked a DIFFERENT task (-20,86,0 → -18,81,-2 → -15,81,-2 → -19,81,-6), zero re-latching; (2) the three y=81 pre-fix-era laps FAILED with missing_material:minecraft:stone_bricks — the mazons palette wants stone BRICKS, the user's chests had plain stone, and the fetch searches within 16 blocks of the ANCHOR (agents.stationRadius default), not of the player — arrival itself worked every time (placement loop only runs within 2 blocks of anchor); (3) comfort:light claimed 01:59:00 completed and vanished from the board — the first full MCP decide→claim→walk→place→auto-complete cycle; (4) -20,86,0 reclaimed at 02:08:16 after its cooldown expired and released again — the standing cooldown loop for a persistently unroutable anchor works as designed (one lap per 5min window). KNOWN EXECUTOR WARTS for a future polish pass: withdrawOnce visits only the FIRST chest in scan order per cycle (a stocked chest behind an unstocked one is invisible); arrival circling when the navigator can't close the last 2 blocks to an anchor (stuck detector only counts UNMOVING ticks — a circling agent moves and evades it; these laps happened to freeze during lag bursts, but a no-progress watchdog is the real fix); board dump shows COMFORT_SHELTER OPEN but the MCP surface hides it (post-SEQ-024 fix confirmed in vivo). Vindication verdict: when walkability + materials line up, the entire S1 chain closes. Next: hot-plug debug access (SEQ-025) would have turned this whole forensics session into a live tap; scenario corpus (Q4) gains its first real-world failure classes: unroutable anchor, missing/wrong material, station-radius ignorance.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"Status: proposed, awaits user go-ahead after the S1-fix retest round.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
