{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T09:00:31.466Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"first real-world failure classes: unroutable anchor, missing/wrong material, station-radius ignorance.`\n\n`SEQ-027 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | HANDOFF | Session wrap. Canonical handoff written: wiki setup/session-handoff-2026-10-17 (supersedes the 2026-10-16 one, which now points forward). It records: S1 live-verified state + full commit chain (2eccf95 gate order, 0f79f43 live fixes, c3318d0 bypass close, 59aa18b hot-plug initiative, 7db0aca SEQ-026), 36/36 gametests, both open initiatives and their remaining items, and the new trap list (per-world serverconfig, javadoc drift, gate-order early-returns, multi-reader gate bypass, reject forensics, mdocs graph backlinks). DEVELOPMENT PAUSE declared by user: next session opens with research — (1) a paper coming out on related Minecraft×LLM research, (2) an existing Minecraft MCP server implementation. Digest questions drafted in the handoff (catalog shape, transport, auth model, session state, loader ecosystem); findings land in a reference/ wiki page before any code resumes. Resume order afterward (user's prior priority): hot-plug P1 tap → corpus Q4 → migration writeup. Tree clean at 7db0aca; mdocs workflow left at EXECUTE with mcp-model-behavior-research active — resume with mdocs_resume and pick up from the handoff.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","oldString":"first real-world failure classes: unroutable anchor, missing/wrong material, station-radius ignorance.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
