{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.818Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"**Update: 2.2.0 does *not* fix this on the native Kimi Code binary — and the 2.2.0 launcher is itself the root cause.** The `node -e \"<inline script>\"` form can never work under Kimi Code's plugin node-runner. Full chain, verified against the installed binary (Kimi Code 2.2.0, macOS arm64):\n\n1. When a plugin declares `command: \"node\"`, Kimi's plugin manager (`withPluginMcpRuntime`) rewrites the spawn to the native binary: `kimi __plugin_run_node <original args…>`, with `cwd` = the plugin root and `KIMI_CODE_HOME` / `KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT` env.\n2. The hidden CLI command is declared as `__plugin_run_node <entry> [args...]`. Commander parses the *first positional* as `<entry>` — so the literal `-e` flag becomes the entry.\n3. `runPluginNodeEntry` (`src/cli/sub/plugin-run-node.ts`) runs `fs.promises.realpath(entry)` → `ENOENT: no such file or directory, realpath '-e'`, prints the bare message to stderr, exits 1.\n4. The MCP client sees the stdio connection close → `MCP error -32000: Connection closed` + that stderr line.\n\nReproduced verbatim by replaying the exact spawn:\n\n```\n$ cd <pluginRoot> && KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT=$PWD kimi __plugin_run_node -e \"<2.2.0 inline script>\"\nENOENT: no such file or directory, realpath '-e'   (exit 1)\n```\n\nThis also means the failure is **not** the relative-path/`MODULE_NOT_FOUND` problem described in the original report — it predates 2.2.0 (the host's log shows the identical error on every session since the plugin was first installed on 2026-09-22).\n\n## Fix (implemented locally, pending release)\n\nThe manifest now launches a real entry file inside the plugin root, which is the only shape Kimi's runner accepts (it enforces `realpath(entry)` + entry-must-be-inside-`KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT`):\n\n- `src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi.plugin.json`: `args` → `[\"./kimi-mcp-entry.js\"]`\n- `src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi-mcp-entry.js` (new): `require(\"./dist/mcp-server.js\").startMcpServer()` — self-locating via `__dirname`, cwd-independent.\n\nVerification, all against the real published artifacts:\n\n- `kimi __plugin_run_node ./kimi-mcp-entry.js` (exact CLI spawn) — initialize, 13-tool `tools/list`, and `mdocs_status` all succeed; plain `node ./kimi-mcp-entry.js` also works.\n- `tests/surfaces/kimi-code`: `plugin.test.ts` updated for the new manifest shape; `launch.test.ts` re-based onto Kimi's actual spawn contract (plugin-root cwd + `MDOCS_PROJECT_DIR` pin) while keeping the original regression guard (managed dir must not collect memory). 55/55 tests pass; `tsc`, `check:versions`, `check:agents`, `npm pack` (file inclusion) all green.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- **Upstream Kimi Code bug:** the `__plugin_run_node` rewrite breaks *any* plugin MCP server using `node -e`/flag-style args. Worth reporting to Moonshot (Kimi Code 2.2.0). Until fixed, manifests must use entry files.\n- **Memory anchoring gap (pre-existing, now reachable):** Kimi spawns plugin MCP servers with `cwd` = plugin root and passes no session-cwd env, so the server anchors memory at the plugin dir via the `cwd` fallback unless the host pins `MDOCS_PROJECT_DIR`. Hooks are unaffected (per-project payloads). The launch test documents this contract; a proper fix needs either Kimi passing the session cwd to plugin MCP spawns or surface-side handling.\n- **Release plan:** the host's managed copy (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs`) was patched in place for immediate relief, but that is ephemeral — cut **2.2.1** from the fixed tree and reinstall the plugin from the updated package path so the managed copy is refreshed.\n\nLeaving the issue open until 2.2.1 is released and a reinstall + new session confirms the fix on the affected host.\n","path":"/tmp/mdocs-issue-10-comment.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.821Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"**Update: 2.2.0 does *not* fix this on the native Kimi Code binary — and the 2.2.0 launcher is itself the root cause.** The `node -e \"<inline script>\"` form can never work under Kimi Code's plugin node-runner. Full chain, verified against the installed binary (Kimi Code 2.2.0, macOS arm64):\n\n1. When a plugin declares `command: \"node\"`, Kimi's plugin manager (`withPluginMcpRuntime`) rewrites the spawn to the native binary: `kimi __plugin_run_node <original args…>`, with `cwd` = the plugin root and `KIMI_CODE_HOME` / `KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT` env.\n2. The hidden CLI command is declared as `__plugin_run_node <entry> [args...]`. Commander parses the *first positional* as `<entry>` — so the literal `-e` flag becomes the entry.\n3. `runPluginNodeEntry` (`src/cli/sub/plugin-run-node.ts`) runs `fs.promises.realpath(entry)` → `ENOENT: no such file or directory, realpath '-e'`, prints the bare message to stderr, exits 1.\n4. The MCP client sees the stdio connection close → `MCP error -32000: Connection closed` + that stderr line.\n\nReproduced verbatim by replaying the exact spawn:\n\n```\n$ cd <pluginRoot> && KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT=$PWD kimi __plugin_run_node -e \"<2.2.0 inline script>\"\nENOENT: no such file or directory, realpath '-e'   (exit 1)\n```\n\nThis also means the failure is **not** the relative-path/`MODULE_NOT_FOUND` problem described in the original report — it predates 2.2.0 (the host's log shows the identical error on every session since the plugin was first installed on 2026-09-22).\n\n## Fix (implemented locally, pending release)\n\nThe manifest now launches a real entry file inside the plugin root, which is the only shape Kimi's runner accepts (it enforces `realpath(entry)` + entry-must-be-inside-`KIMI_PLUGIN_ROOT`):\n\n- `src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi.plugin.json`: `args` → `[\"./kimi-mcp-entry.js\"]`\n- `src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi-mcp-entry.js` (new): `require(\"./dist/mcp-server.js\").startMcpServer()` — self-locating via `__dirname`, cwd-independent.\n\nVerification, all against the real published artifacts:\n\n- `kimi __plugin_run_node ./kimi-mcp-entry.js` (exact CLI spawn) — initialize, 13-tool `tools/list`, and `mdocs_status` all succeed; plain `node ./kimi-mcp-entry.js` also works.\n- `tests/surfaces/kimi-code`: `plugin.test.ts` updated for the new manifest shape; `launch.test.ts` re-based onto Kimi's actual spawn contract (plugin-root cwd + `MDOCS_PROJECT_DIR` pin) while keeping the original regression guard (managed dir must not collect memory). 55/55 tests pass; `tsc`, `check:versions`, `check:agents`, `npm pack` (file inclusion) all green.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- **Upstream Kimi Code bug:** the `__plugin_run_node` rewrite breaks *any* plugin MCP server using `node -e`/flag-style args. Worth reporting to Moonshot (Kimi Code 2.2.0). Until fixed, manifests must use entry files.\n- **Memory anchoring gap (pre-existing, now reachable):** Kimi spawns plugin MCP servers with `cwd` = plugin root and passes no session-cwd env, so the server anchors memory at the plugin dir via the `cwd` fallback unless the host pins `MDOCS_PROJECT_DIR`. Hooks are unaffected (per-project payloads). The launch test documents this contract; a proper fix needs either Kimi passing the session cwd to plugin MCP spawns or surface-side handling.\n- **Release plan:** the host's managed copy (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs`) was patched in place for immediate relief, but that is ephemeral — cut **2.2.1** from the fixed tree and reinstall the plugin from the updated package path so the managed copy is refreshed.\n\nLeaving the issue open until 2.2.1 is released and a reinstall + new session confirms the fix on the affected host.\n","path":"/tmp/mdocs-issue-10-comment.md"}}}
