{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:01:26.572Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-028 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Research pause COMPLETE — three digests, three completed initiatives, all in reference/ wiki. (1) Player-1 paper (arXiv 2610.20584, pixels→RL game control, 38.33% MineDojo-300): exports = verifiable-reward recipe for corpus Q4 (dense score increments over privileged state, invalid-call penalty + wait fallback, reasoning-length penalty, no terminal penalties), randomization axes → corpus diversity axes (targets our failure classes: unroutable anchor / wrong material / station radius), coverage-over-trials metrics with CIs; SFT→RL +34pp vs Base→RL +4pp at equal compute ⇒ sidecar profiles are the value layer for any future usage-derived learning. (2) Minecraft MCP landscape: yuniko server deep-digested (Apache-2.0, Mineflayer protocol-bot, 17 flat verb tools, stdio, NO server-side code) + scan — the whole open MC-MCP ecosystem is that same client-side school; our mod-side registry + sidecar is unrepresented (design validation); multi-client attach unclaimed. Adoption candidates recorded: executor per-move timeout + no-progress watchdog (fixes arrival-circling), hard-reject vs soft-world-no taxonomy + per-field validation messages (corpus Q4 metrics), sidecar stdio hygiene (verified clean), observation ring buffer. (3) JEV + JEVA decision layer: JEV = TypeSafe hosted system-one model (cloud/usage-priced — rejected by user hard constraint); JEVA = open architecture (null-aware/permutation-invariant/option-scalable/cacheable; zero flips in 600-order tests vs Jev 17%/JevK5 26%; 98.66% null AUROC; no weights released). KEY INSIGHT (Prop 2): a \"None\" option inside a flat softmax suffers compulsory -log K drift as the list grows — null must be a SEPARATE coverage question; also no position identifiers. Local alternatives verified for the not-cloud requirement: JevK5-4B GGUF via llama.cpp (Apache-2.0, ~0.6s/short decision on Apple Silicon; weak null recall 0.27-0.46; JevK5-9B regressed vs 4B — don't prefer) and Kev-4B via MLX (Apache-2.0, validated 32GB Macs, 1-255 options, OOD ECE 0.017-0.029; option-order caveat). Tiered recommendation: T0 now = shuffle candidates + separate coverage noul + JEVA metrics (flip rate, all-order accuracy, null AUROC@5%FPR) into corpus Q4 on the existing bonsai path; T1 = self-host JevK5-4B-GGUF or Kev-4B as localhost typed-decision endpoint (task-claim choice, D5-style gate noul, routability coverage), measured on our corpus; T2 = Jeva-style head only if the pattern-tree catalog outgrows T1. Wiki pages: reference/player-1-game-agents, reference/minecraft-mcp-servers, reference/decision-layer-jev-jeva.`\n\n`SEQ-029 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Hot-plug debug access BUILT (initiative mcp-hotplug-debug-access complete; user: \"start building complexity from simple patterns... full visibility and control during development of the next stages\"). P1: sidecar.py --tap <file> — WireTap appends every inbound/outbound protocol line as {\"ts\",\"dir\",\"msg\"} JSONL (append mode; stdout stays protocol-pure — hygiene verified by inspection; tap I/O errors never break the wire; unparsed lines recorded as wire-corruption evidence); sidecar/test_tap.py PASS; README tail recipe. P2: agents.mcp.debugPort (0=off, requires agents.mcp.enabled) → content/mcp/McpDebugServer — loopback-only bind (127.0.0.1), thread-per-connection, READ-ONLY catalog via McpTools.listDescriptor(true) (observe_self/observe_board only) + explicit McpTools.isReadOnly dispatch guard (claim/rest/say rejected BY NAME even when invoked directly), server-thread dispatch like the sidecar channel, lifecycle rides McpSidecar.startFor/stop, bind failure logs and never kills the sidecar. tools/mcp_probe.py stdlib attach client (list|board|self --agent). GAMETESTS 36→38 (McpDebugGameTest: pure gate predicate pinned — never starts when mcp off or port 0; in-JVM socket client over ephemeral port asserting read-only catalog + observe_board on the real board + claim rejected), python bridge + tap tests green. TRAP: gametest structure nbt resolves per class name — new *GameTest class needs its own <classlower>.empty.nbt (copied from an existing one) or the server crashes \"Missing test structure\". Design doc: reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design gained the \"Debug access channel (hot-plug)\" section (open questions resolved: mod-side transport; fresh observe at attach; read-only default; tap format = corpus artifact format). FIRST LIVE USE pending: next dev round tails the tap while the model decides.`\n\n`SEQ-030 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | HANDOFF | Session wrap. Committed: hot-plug code (feat(agents): hot-plug debug access — wire tap + read-only debug transport, SEQ-029) + docs (docs(mdocs): research digests, hot-plug wrap, canonical handoff rewrite, SEQ-028..030). session-handoff-2026-10-17 REWRITTEN in place (was: \"dev pause for research\"; now: research done, hot-plug shipped, next = corpus Q4 → migration writeup → decision-layer T0/T1). mdocs upgraded 2.1.0→2.2.0 (kimi-plugin MCP launch fix note: setup/mdocs-kimi-plugin-fix). New standing trap: drive mdocs via CLI not session MCP tools (in-memory state divergence this session). mdocs valid, 38/38 gametests, workflow at COMPLETE.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio.","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio.","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
