{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:23:12.814Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"CONTEXT","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Map sidecar corpus-relevant code","prompt":"Thoroughness: thorough. Read-only investigation of a NeoForge mod repo's Python \"sidecar\" (MCP bridge between the Minecraft mod and LLM providers). Working dir: /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop.\n\nContext: The next work item is \"corpus Q4\" — a scenario corpus + assertions replayable offline against any endpoint (mock/local LM/cloud), where live-recorded wire-tap files double as recorded artifacts. I need a precise map of what exists today to plan it.\n\nInvestigate and report on:\n\n1. `sidecar/` — every file (catalog.py, model.py, mockmod.py, mcp.py, sidecar.py, run_spike.py, README.md, plus dirs scenarios/, replay/, metrics/, __pycache__). For each: what it does, key classes/functions with signatures, and how they compose (who imports whom).\n2. `sidecar/sidecar.py` in detail: the `--replay` offline mode mechanics, the `--tap <file>` wire-tap format (exact JSONL schema), the decide() flow, prompt vs native tool-calling modes, how observations/board are pulled, how rejects/fallbacks are represented.\n3. `sidecar/run_spike.py`: the A/B runner structure — how scenarios/walks are defined and executed, what WalkResult contains (including the step-level reject forensics mentioned as added for \"the corpus phase\"), what metrics get recorded (metrics/*.jsonl schema).\n4. `sidecar/scenarios/` and `sidecar/replay/` directories: list every file, its schema/format, and how run_spike/sidecar consume them.\n5. Test inventory: sidecar test files (e.g. test_sidecar_bridge.py, tests for tap/replay) — what they cover and how they're run (pytest? stdlib unittest? plain python?).\n6. `mdocs/initiatives/mcp-hotplug-debug-access--2026-10-17.md`: extract the description of the \"three real failure classes\" (unroutable anchor, wrong/missing material, station-radius ignorance) — quote the exact definitions/examples given.\n7. `src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/mcp/` (McpSidecar, McpTools, McpDebugServer): just a 5-line summary of each — what the mod-side catalog/dispatch looks like (tool names, reject shapes), since corpus scenarios must match the mod's real tool surface.\n8. Anything in sidecar/README.md about planned corpus/replay design.\n\nReturn a compact but technically complete report (file:line references). Include the exact tap JSONL schema and an example scenario file contents verbatim if short. Flag anything that looks half-built or TODO-marked for corpus/replay work."}}}
