{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:56:51.308Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Build corpus core + tier0 decide path","prompt":"You are building \"corpus Q4\" for the sidecar of a NeoForge Minecraft mod (repo: /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop). The sidecar is a stdlib-only Python MCP bridge under `sidecar/` that sits between the mod and LLM endpoints. Your job: the scenario corpus + assertions + replay scoring (Player-1 verifiable-reward recipe + JEVA Tier-0 metrics), an experimental Tier-0 decide path, and the corpus runner. A second agent works in parallel on `sidecar/tap_import.py`, `sidecar/test_tap_import.py`, and a small `sidecar/sidecar.py` fix — do NOT touch those three files. Do not touch Java, `mdocs/`, `README.md`, `replay/`, `scenarios/`, or committed `metrics/*.jsonl`.\n\nRead first (under `sidecar/`): `session.py` (Decision, run_decision, WalkResult — you own this file), `model.py` (ModelReply, OpenAiChat, PROFILES/profile_for, FakeModel), `mcp.py` (McpClient, spawn_mock), `mockmod.py` (you own this file), `run_spike.py` (CLI conventions, replay(), summarize()), `catalog.py` (check_args, render_native, render_prompt, first_json_object), `scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json` + `scenarios/dark_room.json` (scenario style), and the \"Corpus Q4 plan (2026-10-17)\" section of `mdocs/initiatives/mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md`. Background: the three live failure classes come from ledger SEQ-024/026 — (1) unroutable anchor: board listed `build:mazons:-20,86,0` (y=86, unpathfindable), model latched onto the first-listed task, claim→stuck-release→reclaim spin; (2) wrong/missing material: mazons palette wants `minecraft:stone_bricks`, the chest held plain `minecraft:stone` → laps failed with missing_material; (3) station-radius ignorance: fetch searches within 16 blocks of the ANCHOR (agents.stationRadius), not the player.\n\nRepo conventions: Python 3.14, stdlib ONLY (no pip, no pytest — tests are plain `python3 <file>.py` scripts that exit non-zero on failure, spawning real subprocesses where needed), dataclasses + light type hints, terse comments only where non-obvious. Match existing code style.\n\n=== SHARED CONTRACT (another agent builds against the scenario schema; keep it exact) ===\n\nCorpus scenario schema (`sidecar/corpus/*.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"unroutable_anchor_first_listed\",\n  \"player_name\": \"Dev\",\n  \"seed\": 41,\n  \"trials\": 8,\n  \"permutations\": 4,\n  \"observation\": \"<multiline [SELF]/[PLAYERS]/[NEARBY BLOCKS]/... string, same style as scenarios/*.json>\",\n  \"open_tasks\": [\n    {\"key\": \"build:mazons:-20,86,0\", \"type\": \"BUILD\", \"detail\": \"small stone-brick house; chest with stone bricks within 16 blocks of anchor\", \"claimable\": true}\n  ],\n  \"assert\": {\"forbid_claim_keys\": [\"build:mazons:-20,86,0\"], \"null_ground_truth\": false, \"notes\": \"unroutable anchor listed first; claiming it = the S1 failure\"}\n}\n```\n- `forbid_claim_keys`: claiming any of these = wrong decision (the encoded failure class).\n- `null_ground_truth`: true iff NO open task is claimable (all forbidden or `claimable:false`).\n- `trials`/`permutations`/`seed` may be overridden by runner CLI flags.\n\nMetrics row (one JSONL line per run, appended to the runner's --out file):\n{\"scenario\",\"trial\",\"permutation\",\"seed\",\"mode\",\"model\",\"tier0\",\"decision_class\",\"chosen_key\",\"correct\",\"failure_class_hit\",\"invalid_reason\",\"coverage_any_claimable\",\"coverage_confidence\",\"completion_tokens\",\"prompt_tokens\",\"latency_ms\",\"reward\",\"board_order\"} — board_order = list of task keys in the order actually shown to the model.\n\n`session.run_decision` NEW SIGNATURE (you implement; keep all existing positional params in order): `run_decision(mode, model, model_tag, client, profile, tier0=False, rng=None)`. `rng` is a `random.Random` the CALLER seeds and owns (do not seed internally). When `tier0=False` the behavior — prompts, tool lists, parse paths, Decision contents — must be IDENTICAL to today.\n\n=== YOUR DELIVERABLES ===\n\n1. `sidecar/session.py`:\n   - `Decision` gains fields with defaults: `coverage_any_claimable: bool | None = None`, `coverage_confidence: float | None = None`, `board_seed: int | None = None`, `board_order: list | None = None`; `to_row()` includes them (board_order -> [] when None).\n   - `run_decision(..., tier0=False, rng=None)`:\n     - Board handling: the open-tasks text shown to the model comes from the mock's `observe_board` result. When `tier0=True`, split that text into per-task lines, shuffle the LINES with `rng` (rng None -> `random.Random()`), record `board_order` = task keys parsed from the shuffled lines (the `key — detail` em-dash format) and `board_seed` = `getattr(rng, \"_seed_placeholder\", None)` is NOT wanted — instead: the caller passes the seed it used via the profile-independent path — add optional param? NO: keep the signature exactly as contracted. Record `board_seed=None` here; the RUNNER writes the real seed into the metrics row (it owns seeding). You only record `board_order`.\n     - Tier-0 coverage question (JEVA: null/coverage is a SEPARATE question, never a list option):\n       - prompt mode: the system/user contract (tier0 variant only) additionally requires a `\"coverage\": {\"any_claimable\": true|false, \"confidence\": <0-100, optional>}` field in the `{\"tool\",\"args\"}` JSON answer. Parse it tolerantly after first_json_object; missing/malformed coverage -> leave `coverage_any_claimable=None` (recorded, not an error, NOT counted invalid).\n       - native mode: tier0 only — the rendered tool schemas carry an extra required boolean `any_claimable` (+ optional number `confidence`) on the effect tools (claim/rest/say); strip these two keys from arguments before `check_args` validation and record them. Use a tier0 variant of `render_native` (e.g. `catalog.render_native(tier0=True)` — you may extend catalog.py IF needed, carefully, default behavior unchanged).\n     - `tier0=False` path: byte-identical to today.\n2. `sidecar/corpus_score.py` — PURE functions (no I/O, no imports from session/mock), operating on plain dicts:\n   - `classify(tool, args, decision_outcome, exec_outcome, model_error)` -> (decision_class, chosen_key, invalid_reason). decision_class ∈ {\"claim\",\"rest\",\"say\",\"wait_fallback\",\"error\"}; invalid_reason set for malformed_json/unknown_tool/bad_args/no_tool_call/model errors (mirror session.py's existing field semantics; an exec reject of a claim (mock/mod `{\"reject\":...}`) yields decision_class \"claim\" with chosen_key set and a marker in invalid_reason like \"exec_reject\" — the claim happened, the world refused it).\n   - `score_run(assert_spec, classified, completion_tokens, budget=512)` -> dict(reward, correct, failure_class_hit). Rules (Player-1 recipe): claim of a claimable, non-forbidden key -> +1 correct; claim of a forbidden key -> 0, failure_class_hit=True; claim rejected by the world (exec_reject, incl. claimable:false) -> 0; rest when null_ground_truth -> +1 correct; rest/say when a permitted claimable task exists -> 0; invalid -> reward -1, decision_class forced \"wait_fallback\" (the wait-fallback penalty), correct False. THEN subtract reasoning-length penalty: `0.005 * max(0, completion_tokens - budget)`, capped at 1.0. No terminal penalties, no clamping beyond the cap.\n   - `jeva_metrics(rows, assert_spec)` where rows share one scenario: flip_rate (fraction of trial-groups — grouped by trial across permutations — whose chosen_key varies across permutations, invalid runs excluded), all_order_accuracy (fraction of permutation runs correct), per-order accuracy, and null-detection confusion matrix over `coverage_any_claimable` vs `null_ground_truth` {tp,fp,tn,fn,tpr,fpr} (rows with coverage None skipped). Document in a module docstring that a binary coverage answer gives no AUROC — a soft `coverage_confidence` is recorded so AUROC becomes computable at Tier 1.\n   - `summarize(rows)` -> per-scenario aggregate: n, mean reward, bootstrap percentile CI (1000 resamples, seeded RNG — deterministic), coverage counts {successes>=1/>=2/>=4 over trials} + booleans.\n3. `sidecar/run_corpus.py` — the runner. CLI: `--corpus PATH` (file or dir of *.json), `--trials N`, `--permutations K`, `--mode {v1,mcp-prompt,mcp-native}` (default mcp-prompt), EITHER `--replay SCRIPT.json` (FakeModel; filter script entries by mode like run_spike.replay does, one FakeModel per run) OR `--endpoint URL --model NAME [--cloud-config F.toml]` (mirror run_spike.py's construction + TOML parse, apiKey never printed), `--tier0`, `--tag NAME`, `--out PATH` (default `metrics/corpus-<tag>-<ts>.jsonl`, cwd-relative append like run_spike), `--quiet`.\n   - Loop: for each scenario: trials = CLI or scenario.trials or 8; perms = CLI or scenario.permutations or 1. Deterministic seeding: `seed = scenario.get(\"seed\", 0) + trial*1000 + perm`; `rng = random.Random(seed)`.\n   - WITHOUT --tier0 and perms>1: pre-permute a deep copy of the scenario's open_tasks with `rng`, write the effective scenario to a temp JSON file (tempfile.mkdtemp, cleaned in finally), spawn the mock against THAT file, and the shown order is the permutation. WITH --tier0: pass the unpermuted scenario; the session-side tier0 shuffle (seeded by your rng) is the order variation; perms still controls how many runs per trial. ALWAYS record `board_order` from the Decision (fallback: the scenario's key order) and the real `seed` in the row.\n   - Per run: spawn mock (mcp.spawn_mock) -> client.start() -> `session.run_decision(mode, model, model_tag, client, profile, tier0=args.tier0, rng=rng)` -> close in finally -> classify + score_run (budget = profile.get(\"budget\", 512) if profile is dict-like else 512) -> append row.\n   - End: print per-scenario x mode summary (n, mean reward, CI, coverage, flip/all-order/null metrics when perms>1 or tier0), mirroring run_spike.summarize's shape. Exit 0 (measurement tool; gating is test_corpus.py's job).\n4. `sidecar/corpus/` — hand-authored scenarios (observation strings modeled on scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json: same census style, poi chest coords consistent with each scenario's detail text; plains day; player Dev):\n   - `unroutable_anchor_first_listed.json`: board lists `build:mazons:-20,86,0` FIRST (detail: small stone-brick house; chest with stone bricks within 16 blocks of anchor; anchor at -20,86,0), then a claimable `comfort:light:...` task. forbid=[the build task], null_ground_truth=false. The observation may carry only ambiguous terrain hints for the anchor area (y=86 is high — the live one was unpathfindable); routability is hidden ground truth, never stated.\n   - `missing_material_stone_vs_bricks.json`: first board task `build:mazons:3a21` whose detail says the palette wants stone BRICKS but the chest holds plain stone (say so in the detail — the model must catch the mismatch; the live failure was exactly this); plus a claimable second task. forbid=[build:mazons:3a21].\n   - `station_radius_edge.json`: two BUILD tasks — `build:mazons:51b0` with chest 14 blocks from anchor (station radius 16, SATISFIABLE — this one is claimable-good) and `build:mazons:62c4` with chest 20 blocks from anchor (BEYOND radius 16 → forbid=[build:mazons:62c4]). Detail text states distances + radius explicitly (v1 tests whether the model uses the numbers).\n   - `null_board_cooling.json`: one task `comfort:light:...` with `claimable:false` (cooling down after release). null_ground_truth=true; correct decision = rest / coverage-no.\n   Each with sensible seed/trials (8)/permutations (4 where order matters, else 1) and a `notes` in assert explaining the failure class.\n5. `sidecar/corpus/gen_variants.py` — seeded variant generator. Do NOT parse prose: build scenarios programmatically from a parameterized template (plains day observation composed from fields: chest pos/contents, station radius, chest distance, board tasks with keys/details). Axes: chest_distance ∈ {8,14,16,18,24}, station_radius ∈ {8,16,24}, materials ∈ {bricks_present, stone_only, empty}, anchor_routable ∈ {true,false} (routability NEVER appears in text), board_order permutations of 2 tasks. `generate(base_fields, count, seed) -> list[dict]` (names encode axis values, e.g. `gen_radius16_dist18_stone`), CLI `--count N --seed S --out-dir corpus/generated/`. forbid/null_ground_truth derived from the axes: a task is forbidden iff (materials not present) OR (chest_distance > station_radius) OR (anchor not routable); null_ground_truth iff all tasks forbidden.\n6. `sidecar/mockmod.py` — ONE behavior addition: `claim` on a task whose scenario entry has `claimable: false` rejects with exactly `\"cooling down after a recent release\"` (the real mod's McpTools.java string family) as a structured `{\"reject\": ...}` outcome, same shape as the existing unknown-key reject. Do not change board rendering, do not add markers; existing scenarios keep identical behavior.\n7. `sidecar/test_corpus.py` — plain-script test (exit non-zero on failure, [PASS]/[FAIL] prints like existing tests):\n   - Unit: score_run across all cases above (correct claim, forbidden hit, exec_reject, null-board rest, missed-opportunity rest, invalid -> -1/wait_fallback, reasoning penalty math incl. the 1.0 cap, budget override).\n   - Unit: jeva_metrics flip/all-order/null-matrix on synthetic row sets (a position-biased row set flips; an invariant set doesn't).\n   - Unit: summarize CI determinism (same seed -> same interval).\n   - Integration via `run_corpus.run(...)` (structure run_corpus so the model is built through an overridable factory or the function accepts a prebuilt model): a `StubClaimFirst` model (mcp-prompt mode; parses the first task key out of the OPEN TASKS text in the last user message; replies with content JSON `{\"tool\":\"claim\",\"args\":{\"task\":\"<first key>\"}}`) and a `StubGood` model (claims the permitted key by matching against a compiled allow-list in the stub, rests on the null board). Drive the 4-scenario corpus with --trials 2 --permutations 2 against a stub. Assert: StubClaimFirst scores ~0 on unroutable_anchor_first_listed with failure_class_hit on every trial AND flips chosen_key across permutations; StubGood scores +1 there and on station_radius_edge (claims 51b0) and null_board_cooling (rest, correct) and misses nothing; StubClaimFirst claiming the cooling task on null_board_cooling lands exec_reject -> wrong. Use tmp --out paths; do not write into the repo's metrics/.\n   - The stubs must satisfy whatever duck-type session.run_decision expects from `model` (read session.py first; ModelReply from model.py).\n\nVerification before you report (ALL must pass, run from `sidecar/`):\n`python3 test_sidecar_bridge.py && python3 test_tap.py && python3 run_spike.py --replay replay/script.json --scenario scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json && python3 run_spike.py --walk --replay replay/walk-script.json --scenario scenarios/walk_build.json && python3 test_corpus.py`\nReport back: files created/changed (with one-line rationale), the exact verification output summary (pass counts), any deviations from this spec and why. If the S0 replay (should be 20/20) or walk replay (3/3) regresses, STOP and fix before reporting."}}}
