entions: Python 3.14, stdlib ONLY (no pip, no pytest — tests are plain `python3 <file>.py` scripts that exit non-zero on failure, spawning real subprocesses where needed), dataclasses + light type hints, terse comments only where non-obvious. Match existing code style.\n\n=== SHARED CONTRACT (another agent builds against the scenario schema; keep it exact) ===\n\nCorpus scenario schema (`sidecar/corpus/*.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"unroutable_anchor_first_listed\",\n  \"player_name\": \"Dev\",\n  \"seed\": 41,\n  \"trials\": 8,\n  \"permutations\": 4,\n  \"observation\": \"<multiline [SELF]/[PLAYERS]/[NEARBY BLOCKS]/... string, same style as scenarios/*.json>\",\n  \"open_tasks\": [\n    {\"key\": \"build:mazons:-20,86,0\", \"type\": \"BUILD\", \"detail\": \"small stone-brick house; chest with stone bricks within 16 blocks of anchor\", \"claimable\": true}\n  ],\n  \"assert\": {\"forbid_claim_keys\": [\"build:mazons:-20,86,0\"], \"null_ground_truth\": false, \"notes\": \"unroutable anchor listed first; claiming it = the S1 failure\"}\n}\n```\n- `forbid_claim_keys`: claiming any of these = wrong decision (the encoded failure class).\n- `null_ground_truth`: true iff NO open task is claimable (all forbidden or `claimable:false`).\n- `trials`/`permutations`/`seed` may be overridden by runner CLI flags.\n\nMetrics row (one JSONL line per run, appended to the runner's --out file):\n{\"scenario\",\"trial\",\"permutation\",\"seed\",\"mode\",\"model\",\"tier0\",\"decision_class\",\"chosen_key\",\"correct\",\"failure_class_hit\",\"invalid_reason\",\"coverage_any_claimable\",\"coverage_confidence\",\"completion_tokens\",\"prompt_tokens\",\"latency_ms\",\"reward\",\"board_order\"} — board_order = list of task keys in the order actually shown to the model.\n\n`session.run_decision` NEW SIGNATURE (you implement; keep all existing positional params in order): `run_decision(mode, model, model_tag, client, profile, tier0=False, rng=None)`. `rng` is a `random.Random` the CALLER seeds and owns (do not seed internally). When `tier0=False` the behavior — prompts, tool lists, parse paths, Decision contents — must be IDENTICAL to today.\n\n=== YOUR DELIVERABLES ===\n\n1. `sidecar/session.py`:\n   - `Decision` gains fields with defaults: `coverage_any_claimable: bool | None = None`, `coverage_confidence: float | None = None`, `board_seed: int | None = None`, `board_order: list | None = None`; `to_row()` includes them (board_order -> [] when None).\n   - `run_decision(..., tier0=False, rng=None)`:\n     - Board handling: the open-tasks text shown to the model comes from the mock's `observe_board` result. When `tier0=True`, split that text into per-task lines, shuffle the LINES with `rng` (rng None -> `random.Random()`), record `board_order` = task keys parsed from the shuffled lines (the `key — detail` em-dash format) and `board_seed` = `getattr(rng, \"_seed_placeholder\", None)` is NOT wanted — instead: the caller passes the seed it used via the profile-independent path — add optional param? NO: keep the signature exactly as contracted. Record `board_seed=None` here; the RUNNER writes the real seed into the metrics row (it owns seeding). You only record `board_order`.\n     - Tier-0 coverage question (JEVA: null/coverage is a SEPARATE question, never a list option):\n       - prompt mode: the system/user contract (tier0 variant only) additionally requires a `\"coverage\": {\"any_claimable\": true|false, \"confidence\": <0-100, optional>}` field in the `{\"tool\",\"args\"}` JSON answer. Parse it tolerantly after first_json_object; missing/malformed coverage -> leave `coverage_any_claimable=None` (recorded, not an error, NOT counted invalid).\n       - native mode: tier0 only — the rendered tool schemas carry an extra required boolean `any_claimable` (+ optional number `confidence`) on the effect tools (claim/rest/say); strip these two keys from arguments before `check_args` validation and record them. Use a tier0 variant of `render_native` (e.g