{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:20:10.507Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Build tap importer + replay fix","prompt":"You are building one slice of \"corpus Q4\" for the sidecar of a NeoForge Minecraft mod (repo: /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop). The sidecar is a stdlib-only Python MCP bridge under `sidecar/`. A second agent works in parallel on `sidecar/session.py`, `sidecar/mockmod.py`, `sidecar/corpus_score.py`, `sidecar/run_corpus.py`, `sidecar/corpus/`, `sidecar/test_corpus.py` — do NOT touch those. Do not touch Java, `mdocs/`, `README.md`, `replay/`, `scenarios/`, or committed `metrics/*.jsonl`.\n\nYour job: (1) a tap→corpus importer that converts a recorded live wire-tap (`sidecar.py --tap`) into a corpus scenario skeleton — this linkage is documented design intent (README P1: \"the tap doubles as the recorded-artifact format for corpus scenarios\") but no code implements it; (2) a small fix to `sidecar.py --replay` so replayed scripts get the real scenario (today it passes an empty dict, so FakeModel `{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` placeholders silently substitute to \"\" / \"Dev\").\n\nRead first (under `sidecar/`): `sidecar.py` (FULL — tap format at lines ~30-52, --replay at ~243-247, decide/serve flow), `model.py` (FakeModel substitution + `modes` filtering), `test_tap.py` and `test_sidecar_bridge.py` (test conventions + how sidecar.py is spawned over crossed pipes), `mockmod.py` (only to understand the board-line format the mock serves), and `mdocs/initiatives/mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md` section \"Corpus Q4 plan (2026-10-17)\".\n\nRepo conventions: Python 3.14, stdlib ONLY (no pip, no pytest — tests are plain `python3 <file>.py` scripts exiting non-zero on failure, using tempfile + subprocess like test_tap.py), dataclasses + light type hints, terse comments only where non-obvious. Match existing code style.\n\n=== SHARED CONTRACT (the other agent builds the corpus against this exact schema — keep it exact) ===\n\nCorpus scenario schema (`sidecar/corpus/*.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"unroutable_anchor_first_listed\",\n  \"player_name\": \"Dev\",\n  \"seed\": 41,\n  \"trials\": 8,\n  \"permutations\": 4,\n  \"observation\": \"<multiline string>\",\n  \"open_tasks\": [\n    {\"key\": \"build:mazons:-20,86,0\", \"type\": \"BUILD\", \"detail\": \"small stone-brick house; ...\", \"claimable\": true}\n  ],\n  \"assert\": {\"forbid_claim_keys\": [\"build:mazons:-20,86,0\"], \"null_ground_truth\": false, \"notes\": \"...\"}\n}\n```\nThe tap→corpus importer emits this shape with the `assert` block left for hand annotation.\n\n=== DELIVERABLE 1: `sidecar/tap_import.py` ===\n\nCLI: `python3 tap_import.py WIRE.jsonl [--out PATH.json]` (print to stdout when --out absent).\n\nInput format — tap JSONL, one object per line: `{\"ts\": \"<UTC ISO-8601>\", \"dir\": \"in\"|\"out\", \"msg\": <parsed JSON-RPC>}` OR `{\"ts\",\"dir\",\"unparsed\": \"<raw line>\"}`. `dir` \"in\" = mod→sidecar, \"out\" = sidecar→mod. Relevant traffic: `tools/call` REQUESTS have `msg.method == \"tools/call\"` with `msg.params.name` (tool name) + `msg.params.arguments`; their RESULTS are `msg.id`-matched objects with `msg.result` (MCP content array; the payload text lives in `result.content[0].text`, JSON-encoded string for mod tool results — inspect `raw` fallback if needed, mirror how sidecar.py's call_mod_tool reads mod-tool results).\n\nExtraction:\n- `observe_self` result content text → the scenario `observation` field (verbatim).\n- `observe_board` result content text → parse board lines into `open_tasks`: each line is `key — detail` (em dash U+2014, the exact format McpTools.java and the mock emit). Split on the FIRST em dash: `{\"key\": <trimmed left>, \"type\": key.split(\":\")[0].upper(), \"detail\": <trimmed right>, \"claimable\": true}`. Lines without an em dash: skip, warn to stderr. If NO line parses, exit 1 with a clear message.\n- The `decide` call's `arguments.agent` (uuid) → used for the scenario name; first tap `ts` also feeds the name.\n- Output JSON (exactly this shape):\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"live-2026-10-17-a1b2c3d4\",\n  \"player_name\": \"Dev\",\n  \"seed\": 0, \"trials\": 8, \"permutations\": 1,\n  \"observation\": \"<observe_self content>\",\n  \"open_tasks\": [ ... ],\n  \"assert\": {\"forbid_claim_keys\": [], \"null_ground_truth\": null, \"notes\": \"TODO hand-annotate ground truth (corpus Q4)\"},\n  \"source\": {\"tap\": \"<input path>\", \"lines\": <n>}\n}\n```\n(name = `live-<first-ts-date>-<first 8 chars of the decide agent uuid>`; fallbacks: no decide call → `live-<date>-unknown`; player_name stays \"Dev\" — do not guess from [PLAYERS].)\n- Robustness: missing observe_self or observe_board → exit 1 with a clear stderr message. `unparsed` lines are skipped silently (they're corrupt wire rows). Multiple decide calls in one tap: use the FIRST complete observe/decide cycle.\n\n=== DELIVERABLE 2: `sidecar/sidecar.py` --replay fix ===\n\nAdd `--scenario PATH` (default `scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json`); load that JSON in the `--replay` branch and pass it as the FakeModel scenario (replacing the current `{}`) so `{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` placeholders resolve. `{{build_key}}` should resolve to the first task key in the scenario (read model.py to see if FakeModel already derives it — if not, that's FakeModel's existing mechanism; do not redesign it, just feed the scenario through). Do not change: the tap writer, serve(), decide() flow, or the non-replay path. `test_sidecar_bridge.py` and `test_tap.py` spawn `sidecar.py --replay replay/bridge-script.json` WITHOUT --scenario — they must pass UNCHANGED (bridge-script uses a literal task key and no placeholders, so feeding the default scenario changes nothing for them; prove it by running them).\n\n=== DELIVERABLE 3: `sidecar/test_tap_import.py` ===\n\nPlain-script test (exit non-zero on failure; [PASS]/[FAIL] prints like test_tap.py):\n- Write a small hand-authored fixture wire.jsonl to a temp dir (~12-15 lines): initialize out/in, notifications/initialized in, tools/call observe_self (id 2, arguments {\"agent\":\"uuid-1\"}) + its result (content[0].text = a short multi-line observation string with [SELF]/[PLAYERS]/[NEARBY BLOCKS] headers), tools/call observe_board (id 3) + result with TWO board lines (`build:mazons:7d2f — small stone-brick house` and `comfort:light:9a41 — dark spot`) plus one garbage line without an em dash (must be skipped with a warning, not crash), one `unparsed` row, and a tools/call decide (id 4, arguments {\"agent\":\"a1b2c3d4-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678\"}) + a simple result. \n- Run the importer (import the module and call its main function, or subprocess — follow test_tap.py's idiom) and assert: name == `live-<date>-a1b2c3d4`, observation matches verbatim, open_tasks has exactly 2 entries with correct key/type/detail/claimable, assert block is the TODO placeholder, source.lines counts all lines.\n- Negative case: a tap with observe_self but no observe_board → non-zero exit.\n\nVerification before you report (from `sidecar/`): `python3 test_sidecar_bridge.py && python3 test_tap.py && python3 test_tap_import.py` — ALL must pass, plus a manual smoke: `python3 tap_import.py <your fixture> ` printing valid JSON (pipe through `python3 -m json.tool` to prove parseability). Report back: files created/changed with one-line rationale, exact verification output summary, any deviations from this spec and why."}}}
