{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:24:14.832Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## Q4: the scenario corpus (model-behavior CI)\n\nQuestion 4 of the research initiative — measurable \"stable behavior\": recorded\nobservations + expected action classes, replayable offline against any endpoint.\nScoring follows the Player-1 verifiable-reward recipe (dense increments; invalid\ncall = penalty + wait fallback; reasoning-length penalty; no terminal penalties)\nplus JEVA Tier-0 metrics (flip rate, all-order accuracy, null-detection matrix —\na binary coverage answer gives no AUROC, so `coverage_confidence` is recorded for\nTier-1 typed endpoints). `corpus/` encodes the three live failure classes from\nledger SEQ-024/026 (unroutable anchor, wrong/missing material, station-radius\nignorance) + a null board; `gen_variants.py` varies chest distance, station\nradius, materials, anchor routability, and board order so assertions test\ninvariance, not one memorized layout. Ground truth lives in each scenario's\n`assert` block (privileged state, never shown to the model).\n\n```bash\n# CI-speed self-tests (stub models, no network): corpus 56 checks + importer\npython3 test_corpus.py && python3 test_tap_import.py\n\n# corpus against a live endpoint (seeded; rows append to metrics/corpus-*.jsonl)\npython3 run_corpus.py --corpus corpus --mode mcp-prompt --trials 8 \\\n    --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1 --model prism-ml/bonsai-27b\n\n# Tier-0 experimental decide path (seeded board shuffle + separate coverage\n# question; OFF by default, byte-identical prompts when off)\npython3 run_corpus.py --corpus corpus/unroutable_anchor_first_listed.json --tier0 \\\n    --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1 --model prism-ml/bonsai-27b --permutations 4\n\n# a recorded live tap becomes a scenario skeleton (ground truth by hand after)\npython3 tap_import.py ../run/wire.jsonl --out corpus/live-draft.json\n```\n\n## Encoded traps (from the ledger — do not relearn)","oldString":"## Encoded traps (from the ledger — do not relearn)","path":"sidecar/README.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:24:14.832Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio. T1 (light task via template fallback) and T2 (build queue) passed earlier in the day. T3 (LLM decision path) exposed four real bugs, all fixed and committed: (1) LM Studio (llama.cpp) rejects response_format \"json_object\" (HTTP 400; only json_schema/text allowed), surfacing client-side as ClosedChannelException — field dropped, system prompt constrains JSON instead (f974a47); (2) dev launchers set -Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system, so localhost resolves ::1-first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of falling back to IPv4, while LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only — endpoint default now 127.0.0.1; reproduced standalone with the same flag (c9ebf8d); (3) reasoning models burn the whole maxTokens budget on hidden thinking (bonsai-27b: 511/511 completion tokens reasoning, empty content, finish_reason=length) — maxTokens default 512->1024, range 16~2048, timeoutSeconds default 30->120, bad_json WARN now includes a 200-char preview of the raw reply (212f147); (4) parseJsonObject required a leading '{' while bonsai answers in json code fences — parser now extracts the first {...} span. Observability added: INFO on LLM decisions + task claims, WARN with reason on fallback, /siasworkshop board debug command. HARD-WON TRAPS: (a) quit-to-menu != client restart — classes and ModConfigSpec bake at JVM start; re-entering the world keeps old code/spec (cost us one full test round); (b) config values outside the RUNNING spec's range are silently \"corrected\" at load — hand-edits beyond the running max get reverted, always re-read the file after load; (c) a commit once claimed a change it didn't contain — verified via javap on build/classes constants; do that when config behaves impossibly. T3 verdict: \"decided via LLM: light {}\" logged twice (13:43:54, 13:44:21) even on the stale 512 spec — intermittent, since reasoning sometimes exceeds 512 (bad_json with empty preview). Reliability needs one true client restart with the 212f147 classes. Model notes: bonsai-27b reasons ~450-900 tokens per decision (60-120s on a loaded M3 Pro); a smaller non-reasoning model is the likely production choice for snappy decisions (config-only switch of llm.model). One isolated http_400 from LM Studio mid-session, unrepeated. Wire-compat writeup: reference/local-llm-feasibility.`\n\n`SEQ-031 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Corpus Q4 BUILT (initiative mcp-model-behavior-research — \"Scenario corpus + assertions for question 4\" checked off; the migration-writeup checkbox remains). Sidecar-only, no Java: corpus_score.py = pure-function Player-1 scoring (+1 correct / 0 wrong / −1 invalid-as-wait_fallback; reasoning-length penalty 0.005/tok capped 1.0 past the profile budget; NO terminal penalties; seeded bootstrap CIs; coverage ≥1/2/4-of-N; JEVA flip rate + all-order accuracy + null confusion matrix — a binary coverage answer gives no AUROC, so coverage_confidence is recorded for Tier-1 typed endpoints); run_corpus.py runner (seeded trials × board permutations vs --replay FakeModel [CI] or any live endpoint; 19-key JSONL rows incl. board_order; non-tier0 permutations materialize temp scenarios, --tier0 lets the session-side seeded shuffle vary order); corpus/ 4 hand-authored failure-class scenarios (unroutable_anchor_first_listed, missing_material_stone_vs_bricks, station_radius_edge, null_board_cooling) + gen_variants.py (5 axes; forbid/null derived from materials × station-radius × routability); tap_import.py converts a --tap wire.jsonl into a corpus skeleton (closes the README-P1 design intent; assert block hand-annotated post-import); test_corpus.py 56 checks + test_tap_import.py. TIER-0 experimental decide path: session.run_decision(..., tier0=False, rng=None) — OFF by default, byte-identical when off (S0 replay 20/20 proof); caller-seeded board-line shuffle recorded as board_order; coverage asked as a SEPARATE question (JEVA Prop 2 — never a list option): prompt mode gains a JSON \"coverage\" object, native mode a required any_claimable bool + optional confidence on effect tools (stripped before check_args). mockmod: claimable:false tasks stay listed (\"listed but not claimable\"), claim rejects with the real mod's exact \"cooling down after a recent release\". BUGS found+fixed en route: (1) catalog.resolve() aliased lists — appending to required[] mutated the shared Tool.inputs, corrupting validation for every later run (now copies; caught by the native-tier0 test); (2) sidecar.py --replay passed {} to FakeModel so {{build_key}}/{{player}} silently became \"\"/\"Dev\" — now --scenario PATH (default scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json). VERIFICATION on the combined tree: python suite all green (bridge, tap, tap-import, S0 replay 20/20, walk 3/3, corpus 56 — incl. position-bias-stub flips-across-permutations + good-stub-invariant integration); ./gradlew build SUCCESSFUL; mdocs valid. Live corpus runs stay manual: next = bonsai tier0 on/off, then Tier-1 JevK5-GGUF/Kev-4B measured on this corpus. Remaining initiative checkbox: the migration recommendation writeup.`","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio. T1 (light task via template fallback) and T2 (build queue) passed earlier in the day. T3 (LLM decision path) exposed four real bugs, all fixed and committed: (1) LM Studio (llama.cpp) rejects response_format \"json_object\" (HTTP 400; only json_schema/text allowed), surfacing client-side as ClosedChannelException — field dropped, system prompt constrains JSON instead (f974a47); (2) dev launchers set -Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system, so localhost resolves ::1-first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of falling back to IPv4, while LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only — endpoint default now 127.0.0.1; reproduced standalone with the same flag (c9ebf8d); (3) reasoning models burn the whole maxTokens budget on hidden thinking (bonsai-27b: 511/511 completion tokens reasoning, empty content, finish_reason=length) — maxTokens default 512->1024, range 16~2048, timeoutSeconds default 30->120, bad_json WARN now includes a 200-char preview of the raw reply (212f147); (4) parseJsonObject required a leading '{' while bonsai answers in json code fences — parser now extracts the first {...} span. Observability added: INFO on LLM decisions + task claims, WARN with reason on fallback, /siasworkshop board debug command. HARD-WON TRAPS: (a) quit-to-menu != client restart — classes and ModConfigSpec bake at JVM start; re-entering the world keeps old code/spec (cost us one full test round); (b) config values outside the RUNNING spec's range are silently \"corrected\" at load — hand-edits beyond the running max get reverted, always re-read the file after load; (c) a commit once claimed a change it didn't contain — verified via javap on build/classes constants; do that when config behaves impossibly. T3 verdict: \"decided via LLM: light {}\" logged twice (13:43:54, 13:44:21) even on the stale 512 spec — intermittent, since reasoning sometimes exceeds 512 (bad_json with empty preview). Reliability needs one true client restart with the 212f147 classes. Model notes: bonsai-27b reasons ~450-900 tokens per decision (60-120s on a loaded M3 Pro); a smaller non-reasoning model is the likely production choice for snappy decisions (config-only switch of llm.model). One isolated http_400 from LM Studio mid-session, unrepeated. Wire-compat writeup: reference/local-llm-feasibility.`","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:24:14.832Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Deliverables:\n- [x] `sidecar/corpus_score.py` — Player-1 scoring: correct decision class\n      = +1; wrong = 0; invalid call (malformed/unknown tool/bad args/no\n      tool_call) = −1 with the decision recorded as `wait_fallback`; minus\n      reasoning-length penalty 0.005/token capped 1.0 beyond the profile\n      budget; no terminal penalties. Aggregation: mean reward, coverage\n      ≥1/2/4-of-N over trials, percentile bootstrap CIs. JEVA metrics: flip\n      rate + all-order accuracy across seeded board permutations; null\n      detection as a confusion matrix at the binary coverage answer (a binary\n      answer gives no AUROC — record any optional confidence field so AUROC\n      becomes computable at Tier 1; document this).\n- [x] `sidecar/run_corpus.py` — runner: loads `corpus/*.json`, runs N seeded\n      trials per scenario against any endpoint (`--replay` FakeModel for CI,\n      `--endpoint/--model` live, cloud config like run_spike), permutation\n      runs when the scenario opts in, rows appended to\n      `metrics/corpus-<tag>-<ts>.jsonl`, per-scenario×mode summary to stdout.\n- [x] `sidecar/corpus/` — three hand-authored scenarios (one per failure\n      class, from the SEQ-024/026 facts) + `gen_variants.py` (seeded generator\n      across the randomization axes: chest distance, station radius, materials\n      present/missing, anchor routability, board order) so assertions test\n      invariance, not one memorized layout. (As built: four scenarios — the\n      null-board-cooling case was needed to exercise `claimable:false`.)\n- [x] Tier-0 experimental decide path (`session.py`,\n      off by default): seeded per-call shuffle of board lines\n      (seed recorded in the metrics row); coverage asked as a separate\n      question — prompt mode gains a `coverage` boolean pair in the JSON\n      contract, native mode gains a required `any_claimable` bool arg on the\n      tier0 decide surface — answers recorded for null-detection metrics.\n      (As built: session.py only; wiring the live bridge `sidecar.py` to the\n      profile flag is deferred — nothing exercises it today.)\n- [x] `sidecar/tap_import.py` (+ test) — convert a recorded `--tap` wire.jsonl\n      into a corpus scenario skeleton (observation + open_tasks from the tap's\n      observe_self/observe_board traffic), `assert` block left for hand\n      annotation.\n- [x] `sidecar/test_corpus.py` (+ `test_tap_import.py`) — scorer unit cases +\n      small-corpus FakeModel regression: a position-biased script (always\n      claims first-listed) must fail the unroutable-anchor scenario and flip\n      across permutations; a good script must pass; repo convention — plain\n      `python3 <file>.py`, exit non-zero on failure.\n- [x] Fix in the corpus path: `sidecar.py --replay` passes an empty scenario\n      dict to FakeModel (`{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` substitute to \"\") —\n      load the scenario file properly. Leave the dead `open_keys` line\n      (sidecar.py:136) for a later cleanup pass.\n- [x] Verification: all six python entry points green (bridge, tap, S0 replay,\n      walk replay, corpus, tap import); `./gradlew build` (no Java changes);\n      `mdocs validate`.","oldString":"Deliverables:\n- [ ] `sidecar/corpus_score.py` — Player-1 scoring: correct decision class\n      = +1; wrong = 0; invalid call (malformed/unknown tool/bad args/no\n      tool_call) = −1 with the decision recorded as `wait_fallback`; minus\n      reasoning-length penalty 0.005/token capped 1.0 beyond the profile\n      budget; no terminal penalties. Aggregation: mean reward, coverage\n      ≥1/2/4-of-N over trials, percentile bootstrap CIs. JEVA metrics: flip\n      rate + all-order accuracy across seeded board permutations; null\n      detection as a confusion matrix at the binary coverage answer (a binary\n      answer gives no AUROC — record any optional confidence field so AUROC\n      becomes computable at Tier 1; document this).\n- [ ] `sidecar/run_corpus.py` — runner: loads `corpus/*.json`, runs N seeded\n      trials per scenario against any endpoint (`--replay` FakeModel for CI,\n      `--endpoint/--model` live, cloud config like run_spike), permutation\n      runs when the scenario opts in, rows appended to\n      `metrics/corpus-<tag>-<ts>.jsonl`, per-scenario×mode summary to stdout.\n- [ ] `sidecar/corpus/` — three hand-authored scenarios (one per failure\n      class, from the SEQ-024/026 facts) + `gen_variants.py` (seeded generator\n      across the randomization axes: chest distance, station radius, materials\n      present/missing, anchor routability, board order) so assertions test\n      invariance, not one memorized layout.\n- [ ] Tier-0 experimental decide path (`session.py`, `sidecar.py`,\n      profile-gated, off by default): seeded per-call shuffle of board lines\n      (seed recorded in the metrics row); coverage asked as a separate\n      question — prompt mode gains a `coverage` boolean pair in the JSON\n      contract, native mode gains a required `any_claimable` bool arg on the\n      tier0 decide surface — answers recorded for null-detection metrics.\n- [ ] `sidecar/tap_import.py` (+ test) — convert a recorded `--tap` wire.jsonl\n      into a corpus scenario skeleton (observation + open_tasks from the tap's\n      observe_self/observe_board traffic), `assert` block left for hand\n      annotation.\n- [ ] `sidecar/test_corpus.py` (+ `test_tap_import.py`) — scorer unit cases +\n      small-corpus FakeModel regression: a position-biased script (always\n      claims first-listed) must fail the unroutable-anchor scenario and flip\n      across permutations; a good script must pass; repo convention — plain\n      `python3 <file>.py`, exit non-zero on failure.\n- [ ] Fix in the corpus path: `sidecar.py --replay` passes an empty scenario\n      dict to FakeModel (`{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` substitute to \"\") —\n      load the scenario file properly. Leave the dead `open_keys` line\n      (sidecar.py:136) for a later cleanup pass.\n- [ ] Verification: all six python entry points green (bridge, tap, S0 replay,\n      walk replay, corpus, tap import); `./gradlew build` (no Java changes);\n      `mdocs validate`.","path":"mdocs/initiatives/mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md"}}}
