{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:24:14.836Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio. T1 (light task via template fallback) and T2 (build queue) passed earlier in the day. T3 (LLM decision path) exposed four real bugs, all fixed and committed: (1) LM Studio (llama.cpp) rejects response_format \"json_object\" (HTTP 400; only json_schema/text allowed), surfacing client-side as ClosedChannelException — field dropped, system prompt constrains JSON instead (f974a47); (2) dev launchers set -Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system, so localhost resolves ::1-first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of falling back to IPv4, while LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only — endpoint default now 127.0.0.1; reproduced standalone with the same flag (c9ebf8d); (3) reasoning models burn the whole maxTokens budget on hidden thinking (bonsai-27b: 511/511 completion tokens reasoning, empty content, finish_reason=length) — maxTokens default 512->1024, range 16~2048, timeoutSeconds default 30->120, bad_json WARN now includes a 200-char preview of the raw reply (212f147); (4) parseJsonObject required a leading '{' while bonsai answers in json code fences — parser now extracts the first {...} span. Observability added: INFO on LLM decisions + task claims, WARN with reason on fallback, /siasworkshop board debug command. HARD-WON TRAPS: (a) quit-to-menu != client restart — classes and ModConfigSpec bake at JVM start; re-entering the world keeps old code/spec (cost us one full test round); (b) config values outside the RUNNING spec's range are silently \"corrected\" at load — hand-edits beyond the running max get reverted, always re-read the file after load; (c) a commit once claimed a change it didn't contain — verified via javap on build/classes constants; do that when config behaves impossibly. T3 verdict: \"decided via LLM: light {}\" logged twice (13:43:54, 13:44:21) even on the stale 512 spec — intermittent, since reasoning sometimes exceeds 512 (bad_json with empty preview). Reliability needs one true client restart with the 212f147 classes. Model notes: bonsai-27b reasons ~450-900 tokens per decision (60-120s on a loaded M3 Pro); a smaller non-reasoning model is the likely production choice for snappy decisions (config-only switch of llm.model). One isolated http_400 from LM Studio mid-session, unrepeated. Wire-compat writeup: reference/local-llm-feasibility.`\n\n`SEQ-031 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Corpus Q4 BUILT (initiative mcp-model-behavior-research — \"Scenario corpus + assertions for question 4\" checked off; the migration-writeup checkbox remains). Sidecar-only, no Java: corpus_score.py = pure-function Player-1 scoring (+1 correct / 0 wrong / −1 invalid-as-wait_fallback; reasoning-length penalty 0.005/tok capped 1.0 past the profile budget; NO terminal penalties; seeded bootstrap CIs; coverage ≥1/2/4-of-N; JEVA flip rate + all-order accuracy + null confusion matrix — a binary coverage answer gives no AUROC, so coverage_confidence is recorded for Tier-1 typed endpoints); run_corpus.py runner (seeded trials × board permutations vs --replay FakeModel [CI] or any live endpoint; 19-key JSONL rows incl. board_order; non-tier0 permutations materialize temp scenarios, --tier0 lets the session-side seeded shuffle vary order); corpus/ 4 hand-authored failure-class scenarios (unroutable_anchor_first_listed, missing_material_stone_vs_bricks, station_radius_edge, null_board_cooling) + gen_variants.py (5 axes; forbid/null derived from materials × station-radius × routability); tap_import.py converts a --tap wire.jsonl into a corpus skeleton (closes the README-P1 design intent; assert block hand-annotated post-import); test_corpus.py 56 checks + test_tap_import.py. TIER-0 experimental decide path: session.run_decision(..., tier0=False, rng=None) — OFF by default, byte-identical when off (S0 replay 20/20 proof); caller-seeded board-line shuffle recorded as board_order; coverage asked as a SEPARATE question (JEVA Prop 2 — never a list option): prompt mode gains a JSON \"coverage\" object, native mode a required any_claimable bool + optional confidence on effect tools (stripped before check_args). mockmod: claimable:false tasks stay listed (\"listed but not claimable\"), claim rejects with the real mod's exact \"cooling down after a recent release\". BUGS found+fixed en route: (1) catalog.resolve() aliased lists — appending to required[] mutated the shared Tool.inputs, corrupting validation for every later run (now copies; caught by the native-tier0 test); (2) sidecar.py --replay passed {} to FakeModel so {{build_key}}/{{player}} silently became \"\"/\"Dev\" — now --scenario PATH (default scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json). VERIFICATION on the combined tree: python suite all green (bridge, tap, tap-import, S0 replay 20/20, walk 3/3, corpus 56 — incl. position-bias-stub flips-across-permutations + good-stub-invariant integration); ./gradlew build SUCCESSFUL; mdocs valid. Live corpus runs stay manual: next = bonsai tier0 on/off, then Tier-1 JevK5-GGUF/Kev-4B measured on this corpus. Remaining initiative checkbox: the migration recommendation writeup.`","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED against real LM Studio. T1 (light task via template fallback) and T2 (build queue) passed earlier in the day. T3 (LLM decision path) exposed four real bugs, all fixed and committed: (1) LM Studio (llama.cpp) rejects response_format \"json_object\" (HTTP 400; only json_schema/text allowed), surfacing client-side as ClosedChannelException — field dropped, system prompt constrains JSON instead (f974a47); (2) dev launchers set -Djava.net.preferIPv6Addresses=system, so localhost resolves ::1-first and java.net.http fails fast with ClosedChannelException instead of falling back to IPv4, while LM Studio binds 127.0.0.1 only — endpoint default now 127.0.0.1; reproduced standalone with the same flag (c9ebf8d); (3) reasoning models burn the whole maxTokens budget on hidden thinking (bonsai-27b: 511/511 completion tokens reasoning, empty content, finish_reason=length) — maxTokens default 512->1024, range 16~2048, timeoutSeconds default 30->120, bad_json WARN now includes a 200-char preview of the raw reply (212f147); (4) parseJsonObject required a leading '{' while bonsai answers in json code fences — parser now extracts the first {...} span. Observability added: INFO on LLM decisions + task claims, WARN with reason on fallback, /siasworkshop board debug command. HARD-WON TRAPS: (a) quit-to-menu != client restart — classes and ModConfigSpec bake at JVM start; re-entering the world keeps old code/spec (cost us one full test round); (b) config values outside the RUNNING spec's range are silently \"corrected\" at load — hand-edits beyond the running max get reverted, always re-read the file after load; (c) a commit once claimed a change it didn't contain — verified via javap on build/classes constants; do that when config behaves impossibly. T3 verdict: \"decided via LLM: light {}\" logged twice (13:43:54, 13:44:21) even on the stale 512 spec — intermittent, since reasoning sometimes exceeds 512 (bad_json with empty preview). Reliability needs one true client restart with the 212f147 classes. Model notes: bonsai-27b reasons ~450-900 tokens per decision (60-120s on a loaded M3 Pro); a smaller non-reasoning model is the likely production choice for snappy decisions (config-only switch of llm.model). One isolated http_400 from LM Studio mid-session, unrepeated. Wire-compat writeup: reference/local-llm-feasibility.`","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:24:14.836Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Deliverables:\n- [x] `sidecar/corpus_score.py` — Player-1 scoring: correct decision class\n      = +1; wrong = 0; invalid call (malformed/unknown tool/bad args/no\n      tool_call) = −1 with the decision recorded as `wait_fallback`; minus\n      reasoning-length penalty 0.005/token capped 1.0 beyond the profile\n      budget; no terminal penalties. Aggregation: mean reward, coverage\n      ≥1/2/4-of-N over trials, percentile bootstrap CIs. JEVA metrics: flip\n      rate + all-order accuracy across seeded board permutations; null\n      detection as a confusion matrix at the binary coverage answer (a binary\n      answer gives no AUROC — record any optional confidence field so AUROC\n      becomes computable at Tier 1; document this).\n- [x] `sidecar/run_corpus.py` — runner: loads `corpus/*.json`, runs N seeded\n      trials per scenario against any endpoint (`--replay` FakeModel for CI,\n      `--endpoint/--model` live, cloud config like run_spike), permutation\n      runs when the scenario opts in, rows appended to\n      `metrics/corpus-<tag>-<ts>.jsonl`, per-scenario×mode summary to stdout.\n- [x] `sidecar/corpus/` — three hand-authored scenarios (one per failure\n      class, from the SEQ-024/026 facts) + `gen_variants.py` (seeded generator\n      across the randomization axes: chest distance, station radius, materials\n      present/missing, anchor routability, board order) so assertions test\n      invariance, not one memorized layout. (As built: four scenarios — the\n      null-board-cooling case was needed to exercise `claimable:false`.)\n- [x] Tier-0 experimental decide path (`session.py`,\n      off by default): seeded per-call shuffle of board lines\n      (seed recorded in the metrics row); coverage asked as a separate\n      question — prompt mode gains a `coverage` boolean pair in the JSON\n      contract, native mode gains a required `any_claimable` bool arg on the\n      tier0 decide surface — answers recorded for null-detection metrics.\n      (As built: session.py only; wiring the live bridge `sidecar.py` to the\n      profile flag is deferred — nothing exercises it today.)\n- [x] `sidecar/tap_import.py` (+ test) — convert a recorded `--tap` wire.jsonl\n      into a corpus scenario skeleton (observation + open_tasks from the tap's\n      observe_self/observe_board traffic), `assert` block left for hand\n      annotation.\n- [x] `sidecar/test_corpus.py` (+ `test_tap_import.py`) — scorer unit cases +\n      small-corpus FakeModel regression: a position-biased script (always\n      claims first-listed) must fail the unroutable-anchor scenario and flip\n      across permutations; a good script must pass; repo convention — plain\n      `python3 <file>.py`, exit non-zero on failure.\n- [x] Fix in the corpus path: `sidecar.py --replay` passes an empty scenario\n      dict to FakeModel (`{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` substitute to \"\") —\n      load the scenario file properly. Leave the dead `open_keys` line\n      (sidecar.py:136) for a later cleanup pass.\n- [x] Verification: all six python entry points green (bridge, tap, S0 replay,\n      walk replay, corpus, tap import); `./gradlew build` (no Java changes);\n      `mdocs validate`.","oldString":"Deliverables:\n- [ ] `sidecar/corpus_score.py` — Player-1 scoring: correct decision class\n      = +1; wrong = 0; invalid call (malformed/unknown tool/bad args/no\n      tool_call) = −1 with the decision recorded as `wait_fallback`; minus\n      reasoning-length penalty 0.005/token capped 1.0 beyond the profile\n      budget; no terminal penalties. Aggregation: mean reward, coverage\n      ≥1/2/4-of-N over trials, percentile bootstrap CIs. JEVA metrics: flip\n      rate + all-order accuracy across seeded board permutations; null\n      detection as a confusion matrix at the binary coverage answer (a binary\n      answer gives no AUROC — record any optional confidence field so AUROC\n      becomes computable at Tier 1; document this).\n- [ ] `sidecar/run_corpus.py` — runner: loads `corpus/*.json`, runs N seeded\n      trials per scenario against any endpoint (`--replay` FakeModel for CI,\n      `--endpoint/--model` live, cloud config like run_spike), permutation\n      runs when the scenario opts in, rows appended to\n      `metrics/corpus-<tag>-<ts>.jsonl`, per-scenario×mode summary to stdout.\n- [ ] `sidecar/corpus/` — three hand-authored scenarios (one per failure\n      class, from the SEQ-024/026 facts) + `gen_variants.py` (seeded generator\n      across the randomization axes: chest distance, station radius, materials\n      present/missing, anchor routability, board order) so assertions test\n      invariance, not one memorized layout.\n- [ ] Tier-0 experimental decide path (`session.py`, `sidecar.py`,\n      profile-gated, off by default): seeded per-call shuffle of board lines\n      (seed recorded in the metrics row); coverage asked as a separate\n      question — prompt mode gains a `coverage` boolean pair in the JSON\n      contract, native mode gains a required `any_claimable` bool arg on the\n      tier0 decide surface — answers recorded for null-detection metrics.\n- [ ] `sidecar/tap_import.py` (+ test) — convert a recorded `--tap` wire.jsonl\n      into a corpus scenario skeleton (observation + open_tasks from the tap's\n      observe_self/observe_board traffic), `assert` block left for hand\n      annotation.\n- [ ] `sidecar/test_corpus.py` (+ `test_tap_import.py`) — scorer unit cases +\n      small-corpus FakeModel regression: a position-biased script (always\n      claims first-listed) must fail the unroutable-anchor scenario and flip\n      across permutations; a good script must pass; repo convention — plain\n      `python3 <file>.py`, exit non-zero on failure.\n- [ ] Fix in the corpus path: `sidecar.py --replay` passes an empty scenario\n      dict to FakeModel (`{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}` substitute to \"\") —\n      load the scenario file properly. Leave the dead `open_keys` line\n      (sidecar.py:136) for a later cleanup pass.\n- [ ] Verification: all six python entry points green (bridge, tap, S0 replay,\n      walk replay, corpus, tap import); `./gradlew build` (no Java changes);\n      `mdocs validate`.","path":"mdocs/initiatives/mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:25:04.346Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"      Local (bonsai-27b, n=1/mode): v1 FAILED (120s timeout; previous run\n      empty_content:length at 1024 — 2/2 budget burnouts on the v1 prompt) while\n      BOTH MCP modes succeeded (~39s, ~350-390 tokens). LM Studio accepted native\n      tool-calling for bonsai. Details + findings: ledger SEQ-020; sidecar/README.md;\n      metrics in sidecar/metrics-*.jsonl.\n- [2026-10-17] Corpus Q4 done (evening; two parallel builder agents, coordinator\n      re-verified on the combined tree). Delivered: `corpus_score.py` (pure-function\n      Player-1 scoring + seeded bootstrap CIs + JEVA flip/all-order/null-matrix;\n      binary coverage answer gives no AUROC — `coverage_confidence` recorded for\n      Tier 1), `run_corpus.py` (seeded trials × board permutations vs `--replay`\n      FakeModel or any live endpoint; 19-key JSONL rows incl. `board_order`),\n      `corpus/` 4 hand-authored failure-class scenarios + `gen_variants.py`\n      (5 randomization axes; forbid/null derived from materials × radius ×\n      routability), `tap_import.py` (wire.jsonl → corpus skeleton; closes the\n      README-P1 intent), `test_corpus.py` 56 checks + `test_tap_import.py`.\n      Tier-0 experimental decide path: `session.run_decision(..., tier0=False,\n      rng=None)` — caller-seeded board shuffle + coverage as a SEPARATE question\n      (prompt JSON `coverage` object / native required `any_claimable` + optional\n      `confidence`, stripped pre-validation); tier0=False byte-identical (S0 replay\n      20/20 proof). mockmod: `claimable:false` tasks listed, claim rejects with the\n      real mod's cooldown string. Fixed en route: `catalog.resolve()` list aliasing\n      (mutated shared `Tool.inputs`); `sidecar.py --replay` gained `--scenario`\n      (FakeModel placeholders were silently empty). Verification: python suite all\n      green (bridge/tap/tap-import/S0 20-20/walk 3-3/corpus 56), `./gradlew build`\n      SUCCESSFUL, mdocs valid. Live corpus runs are manual (next: bonsai tier0\n      on/off, then Tier-1 JevK5/Kev-4B). Ledger SEQ-031. Remaining checkbox: the\n      migration recommendation writeup.","oldString":"      Local (bonsai-27b, n=1/mode): v1 FAILED (120s timeout; previous run\n      empty_content:length at 1024 — 2/2 budget burnouts on the v1 prompt) while\n      BOTH MCP modes succeeded (~39s, ~350-390 tokens). LM Studio accepted native\n      tool-calling for bonsai. Details + findings: ledger SEQ-020; sidecar/README.md;\n      metrics in sidecar/metrics-*.jsonl.","path":"mdocs/initiatives/mcp-model-behavior-research-2026-10-15--2026-10-15.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:25:04.346Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"REPORT","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"---\nid: \"session-handoff-2026-10-17\"\ntitle: \"Session Handoff — 2026-10-17 (corpus Q4 built; next: migration writeup, then Tier-1)\"\ncategory: \"setup\"\ncreated: \"2026-10-17\"\nupdated: \"2026-10-17\"\nrelated_initiatives: [\"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15\", \"mcp-hotplug-debug-access--2026-10-17\", \"research-digest-player-1-synthetic-game-agents--2026-10-17\", \"research-digest-jev-jeva-decision-layer--2026-10-17\"]\ntags: [\"handoff\",\"agents\",\"llm\",\"mcp\",\"session-state\"]\nlifecycle: \"stable\"\nknowledge_type: \"reference\"\nconfidence: \"high\"\nsource_initiatives: []\n---\n\n# Session handoff — read this first (current)\n\nCanonical handoff as of 2026-10-17 late evening (third revision of this file\ntoday). Revision history: v1 \"S1 live-verified; dev pause for research\"\n(pre-pause story now in `session-handoff-2026-10-16` + ledger SEQ-020..026) →\nv2 \"research digests done; hot-plug built; next: corpus Q4\" → v3 (this):\n**corpus Q4 shipped; next is the migration writeup, then Tier-1 evaluation.**\n\n**STATUS: development ACTIVE.** Next code move is the **migration\nrecommendation writeup** → `reference/` wiki (closes the research initiative;\nits last open checkbox). Then Tier-1 (self-hosted JevK5/Kev-4B measured on the\ncorpus) and live bonsai tier0 on/off runs.\n\nReading order for a fresh agent:\n1. `AGENTS.md`, then this file.\n2. `setup/agent-shared-ledger` — SEQ-028 (digests), SEQ-029 (hot-plug),\n   SEQ-030 (v2 wrap), **SEQ-031 (corpus Q4, this wrap's work)**.\n3. The three digest pages: `reference/player-1-game-agents`,\n   `reference/minecraft-mcp-servers`, `reference/decision-layer-jev-jeva`.\n4. Initiative `mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15` — one open workstream,\n   ONE checkbox left (migration writeup). The \"Corpus Q4 plan (2026-10-17)\"\n   section is fully ticked; Progress Log has the as-built record.\n5. `reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design` — includes the \"Debug access channel\n   (hot-plug)\" section.\n6. `sidecar/README.md` — new \"Q4: the scenario corpus\" section has the run\n   commands (corpus runner, tier0, tap import).\n\n## Where things stand\n\n- **Research pause: COMPLETE** (three digests; see SEQ-028 for the one-paragraph\n  summary of all three + the tiered T0/T1/T2 recommendation).\n- **Hot-plug debug access: DONE** (SEQ-029): `--tap` wire tap +\n  `agents.mcp.debugPort` read-only attach; 38/38 gametests.\n- **Corpus Q4: DONE** (SEQ-031, evening build; sidecar-only, no Java):\n  - `corpus_score.py` — pure-function Player-1 scoring (+1/0/−1-wait-fallback,\n    reasoning-length penalty capped 1.0, no terminal penalties, seeded bootstrap\n    CIs, coverage ≥1/2/4) + JEVA metrics (flip rate, all-order accuracy,\n    null-detection matrix; binary coverage gives no AUROC — `coverage_confidence`\n    recorded so Tier-1 typed endpoints can compute it).\n  - `run_corpus.py` — seeded trials × board permutations against `--replay`\n    FakeModel (CI) or any live endpoint; 19-key JSONL rows incl. `board_order`.\n  - `corpus/` — 4 hand-authored scenarios encoding the three live failure\n    classes (unroutable anchor first-listed, stone-vs-bricks material mismatch,\n    station-radius edge, null board w/ cooling task) + `gen_variants.py`\n    (5 randomization axes; forbid/null derived from materials × radius ×\n    routability).\n  - `tap_import.py` — a recorded `--tap` wire.jsonl becomes a corpus scenario\n    skeleton (README-P1 design intent now real; ground truth hand-annotated).\n  - Tier-0 experimental decide path: `session.run_decision(..., tier0=False,\n    rng=None)` — seeded board shuffle + coverage as a SEPARATE question (JEVA\n    Prop 2); OFF by default, byte-identical when off (20/20 replay proof).\n  - Tests: `test_corpus.py` 56 checks (incl. position-bias-stub flips across\n    permutations / good-stub invariant integration) + `test_tap_import.py`.\n  - En-route fixes: `catalog.resolve()` list aliasing (corrupted shared\n    `Tool.inputs`); `sidecar.py --replay --scenario` (FakeModel placeholders\n    were silently empty).\n- **Known executor warts** (unchanged, queued polish): `withdrawOnce` visits\n  only the FIRST chest in scan order; arrival-circling evades the stuck\n  detector (no-progress watchdog is the real fix — adoption candidate from the\n  MCP-landscape digest).\n- **Open workstream**: `mcp-model-behavior-research` — remaining: the\n  migration recommendation writeup ONLY. Live corpus runs (bonsai tier0 on/off,\n  then Tier-1 endpoints) are manual measurement sessions, not build work.\n\n## Next moves (priority order)\n\n1. **Migration recommendation** → `reference/` wiki: LlmClient→MCP-client\n   migration plan (config: sidecar address instead of endpoint/model/apiKey).\n   Closes the research initiative. All inputs exist (SEQ-020..024, S0-S2\n   results, hot-plug operational experience).\n2. **Live corpus measurement**: `run_corpus.py --corpus corpus --trials 8`\n   against bonsai (tier0 off vs on) — first real numbers for the Tier-0\n   prompt factorization; then JevK5-4B-GGUF / Kev-4B (Tier-1) on the same\n   corpus.\n3. **Executor wart polish** (independent): multi-chest `withdrawOnce`,\n   no-progress watchdog.\n4. Ops (question 5, whenever): Gradle/CI wiring for the corpus runner.\n\n## Traps that cost real time (accumulated; S1-era ones still apply)\n\n- **Server configs are PER-WORLD** (`<world>/serverconfig/`): seed\n  `run/defaultconfigs/siasworkshop-server.toml` AND copy into existing worlds.\n- **Javadoc-vs-code drift is real**; **gate-order bugs hide in early-returns**\n  (pin pure routing fns); **list-filter fixes are bypassable by second readers**\n  (enumerate EVERY caller); **reject payloads must carry their reason**.\n- **mdocs state: drive the CLI, not the session MCP tools.** Details:\n  `setup/mdocs-kimi-plugin-fix`.\n- **Gametest structure files resolve per class name**: a new `*GameTest` class\n  needs `src/main/resources/data/siasworkshop/structure/<classlower>.empty.nbt`\n  (copy an existing one) or the server crashes with \"Missing test structure\".\n- **Validator reciprocal backlinks**: every `related_wiki` entry on an\n  initiative needs the initiative id in the page's `related_initiatives`, and\n  vice versa — validate before claiming done.\n- Gametests are 38; same standing traps (no `@GameTest(timeout=)`, shared batch\n  world, production tick loop runs during tests, claim your OWN key).\n- **Python suite is now SIX entry points** (run from `sidecar/`):\n  `test_sidecar_bridge.py`, `test_tap.py`, `test_tap_import.py`,\n  `run_spike.py --replay replay/script.json`,\n  `run_spike.py --walk --replay replay/walk-script.json`, `test_corpus.py`.\n- **NEW (SEQ-031): never extend `catalog.resolve()` output in place** — it now\n  copies lists because appending to a resolved `required[]` mutated the shared\n  `Tool.inputs` for every later run. Same class of bug as the list-aliasing\n  trap: resolve-then-mutate is a corruption vector.\n- **NEW (SEQ-031): `FakeModel` placeholders need the real scenario** —\n  `sidecar.py --replay` now takes `--scenario` (default\n  `scenarios/stone_bricks_chest.json`); without it `{{build_key}}`/`{{player}}`\n  silently substitute to `\"\"`/`\"Dev\"`.\n\n## Environment facts\n\n- M3 Max; LM Studio local (`http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`, `prism-ml/bonsai-27b` —\n  reasoning model, 30–90s per MCP decision under load). Game + model on one\n  machine = constant \"Can't keep up\" bursts.\n- Live-test recipe: full JVM restart, world TestSidecar01, `agents.mcp.enabled=true`\n  with the ABSOLUTE sidecar path in its serverconfig; raise a build task with\n  stone-bricks chest ≤16 blocks of the anchor; watch `sidecar started (pid …)`\n  then `decided via MCP sidecar`. Add `--tap /abs/path/run/wire.jsonl` to the\n  command for forensics-free rounds; convert the tap afterwards with\n  `python3 sidecar/tap_import.py run/wire.jsonl --out sidecar/corpus/live-….json`\n  (hand-annotate the `assert` block).\n- The TestSidecar01 board still holds the unroutable `build:mazons:-20,86,0` —\n  burns one agent lap per 5-min cooldown window; cosmetic. It is also the\n  anchor of corpus scenario `unroutable_anchor_first_listed`.\n- mdocs: after ANY hand-edit under `mdocs/`: `./node_modules/.bin/mdocs validate`.\n","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/session-handoff-2026-10-17.md"}}}
