→ all rows correct, reward +1, board_order varies with permutation, coverage_any_claimable False on the null board.\n2. Option-order caveat: scripted policy keyed to ORDER (claims the FIRST option in whatever order it receives; P(yes) always 0.9) → chosen_key flips across permutations (flip_rate 1.0 via corpus_score.jeva_metrics), failure_class_hit on unroutable trials.\n3. null_auc: mixed synthetic rows (perfect separation, reversed, single-class → None).\n4. Wire mismatch: stub returns {\"unexpected\": true} → the parse error names the top-level keys (assert the error message mentions them).\n5. Transport failure: http_post raising ConnectionError → row recorded with invalid_reason and reward -1 (run continues, exit still 0; assert the row).\nUse tmp --out paths; never write into the repo's metrics/.\n\nVerification before reporting (from `sidecar/`): `python3 test_decision_probe.py && python3 test_corpus.py && python3 test_tap_import.py` — all must pass (test_corpus.py must still be 56 checks green; do not weaken existing tests). Report: files changed, exact verification output summary, any deviations from this spec and why."}}}
