{"timestamp":"2026-10-18T04:52:52.062Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"VERIFY","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Remaining initiative checkbox: the migration recommendation writeup.`\n\n`SEQ-032 | 2026-10-17 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Tier-1 typed-decision spike MEASURED on the corpus Q4 instrument (user-triggered: \"test on lm studio first, integrate later; maybe bundle — it's tiny\"). LM STUDIO RULED OUT AS SERVER by the model cards: Kev = prefill-only decision scorer + pointer head + custom MLX runtime — \"stock llama.cpp/transformers/mlx-lm cannot load this artifact\", chat is an explicit out-of-scope use, and LM Studio's own kev download lacked runtime/ (it remains a fine download mechanism). Served OUT of repo: Jakevin/kev-4b-ternary-mlx v2.0 on 127.0.0.1:8010 (included runtime, 1.7GB, decision-v7 dev 0.8647 vs bf16 0.8718) + chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-0.8B-Decision-v3-MLX 8bit on :8011 (jev-style[mlx] PyPI pkg, 0.80GB); uv-managed py3.13 venv ~/.venvs/kev (system python is 3.14; runtimes want 3.12/3.13). WIRES IDENTICAL: answers.{name}.{type,choice,confidence,probabilities}, noul as bare P(yes), usage.input/output_tokens — probe_decision.py needed one parser fix (noul key + input/output_tokens aliases; tests re-verified). BUILT: probe_decision.py (corpus → SystemOne renderer; ONE request with TWO isolated questions — claim choice over the seeded option order + coverage noul, JEVA factorization native to the API, no position identifiers; derived decision gates the claim on P(yes)>=0.5; rows extend the 19-key corpus schema with option_probs + p_yes; 52 stub-server checks) + corpus_score.null_auc (Mann-Whitney AUC + TPR@~5%FPR over soft coverage scores — the metric the binary LLM path couldn't compute) + test_decision_probe.py. LIVE: 104 seeded runs per endpoint over the 4 failure-class scenarios. RESULTS — Jev-Style-0.8B: argmax picks the FORBIDDEN task 96/96 non-null runs (unroutable/missing-material/station ALL stably inverted — not position noise: probability mass swings 0.22-0.78 with option order but argmax tracks content WRONG), coverage polarity inverted (cross-scenario null AUC 0.0, TPR@5%FPR 0.0); its single +1 (null board) was a 0.5-gate artifact (P(yes)=0.333<0.5 -> rest). Kev-ternary-v2: choice content signal REAL — argmax permitted 32/32 unroutable + 32/32 station-radius (the two classes bonsai-27b failed live in SEQ-024/026!), 18/32 missing-material (stone-vs-bricks nuance flips its coin; argmax-flip 6/8 trials) — but coverage at OOD indifference: P(yes) 0.45-0.48 on claimable boards vs 0.563 on the null board, so unroutable+station derived \"rest\" (reward 0 DESPITE the right argmax — missed opportunity) and null derived \"claim\" (0). A domain recalibration (threshold ~0.44; principled version = the card's own kev.calibrate on our labels) flips 3/4 scenarios to correct. VERDICT: no drop-in win — typed endpoints need recalibration/fine-tuning on our domain; Tier-1 continues only as kev+recalibrate (jev-style's 5x size advantage does not offset total inversion); the LLM tier0 path stays the production answer; corpus Q4 + probe_decision.py is now the standing instrument for any future candidate (incl. JevK5-4B-GGUF and post-recalibration re-runs — models remain in ~/.cache, venv in ~/.venvs/kev). Distribution idea (user: bundle a tiny decision model in the mod install) RECORDED, discussion deferred — hard constraint: in-mod Java inference of a 0.8-4B model is not realistic; plausible shapes = sidecar-bundled loopback endpoint / external-runtime dependency / ONNX export + in-mod runtime; decide with recalibrated numbers. Suite: 7 python entry points green (probe added; bridge/tap/tap-import/S0 20-20/walk 3-3/corpus 56/probe 52); servers stopped. Metrics: sidecar/metrics/corpus-kev-ternary-v2-20261017-224454.jsonl, sidecar/metrics/corpus-jevstyle-0.8b-v3-8bit-20261017-224552.jsonl.`\n\n## Referenced By","oldString":"Remaining initiative checkbox: the migration recommendation writeup.`\n\n## Referenced By","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
