initiative Progress Log).\n4. **Live bonsai tier0 on/off corpus run** — first real Tier-0 factorization\n   numbers (`python3 sidecar/run_corpus.py --corpus sidecar/corpus --endpoint\n   http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1 --model prism-ml/bonsai-27b [--tier0]`).\n5. Ops (question 5, whenever): Gradle/CI wiring for the corpus runner.","oldString":"- **Known executor warts** (unchanged, queued polish): `withdrawOnce` visits\n  only the FIRST chest in scan order; arrival-circling evades the stuck\n  detector (no-progress watchdog is the real fix — adoption candidate from the\n  MCP-landscape digest).\n- **Open workstream**: `mcp-model-behavior-research` — remaining: the\n  migration recommendation writeup ONLY. Live corpus runs (bonsai tier0 on/off,\n  then Tier-1 endpoints) are manual measurement sessions, not build work.\n\n## Next moves (priority order)\n\n1. **Migration recommendation** → `reference/` wiki: LlmClient→MCP-client\n   migration plan (config: sidecar address instead of endpoint/model/apiKey).\n   Closes the research initiative. All inputs exist (SEQ-020..024, S0-S2\n   results, hot-plug operational experience).\n2. **Live corpus measurement**: `run_corpus.py --corpus corpus --trials 8`\n   against bonsai (tier0 off vs on) — first real numbers for the Tier-0\n   prompt factorization; then JevK5-4B-GGUF / Kev-4B (Tier-1) on the same\n   corpus.\n3. **Executor wart polish** (independent): multi-chest `withdrawOnce`,\n   no-progress watchdog.\n4. Ops (question 5, whenever): Gradle/CI wiring for the corpus runner.","path":"/Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop/mdocs/wiki/setup/session-handoff-2026-10-17.md"}}}
