{"timestamp":"2026-10-20T07:05:07.481Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"Nothing committed — tree holds the full changeset.`\n\n`SEQ-034 | 2026-10-20 | coordinator | RESOLVED | LIVE TEST-RUN SESSION (protocol setup/test-run-protocol-2026-10-20; user launched LM Studio, prism-ml/bonsai-27b on :1234). Phase 0: 7/7 python entry points green + FakeModel corpus demo (position-bias stub caught precisely: unroutable 0.000 across orders, station flip_rate 1.00). Phase 1: kev-4b-ternary v2.0 re-served (:8010, venv ~/.venvs/kev, prefix cache) and probe_decision re-ran 104 seeded decisions — SEQ-032 VERDICT REPROUCED EXACTLY: argmax right 32/32 unroutable (reachable light task) + 32/32 station-radius (in-radius anchor), coin-flip 18/32 stone-vs-bricks; coverage gate at OOD indifference P(yes) 0.45-0.49 claimable vs 0.563 null → 96 missed-claim rests + 8 null-board claim leaks, mean_reward 0 everywhere (metrics/corpus-kev-live-20261020-20261020-002538.jsonl). Phase 2a — FIRST LIVE BONSAI TIER-0 NUMBERS (the queued Tier-0 factorization measurement; 4 scenarios × trials 4 × perms 2 = 28 decisions/mode, paired seeds, mode mcp-prompt, ~35 min both modes): TIER0 OFF — bonsai CRUSHED the claimable scenarios (missing_material +1.000 all_order 1.00, station_radius +0.861, unroutable +0.978, flip_rate 0.00 everywhere — choices fully order-invariant) but CLAIMED THE NULL BOARD 8/8 (the standing null leak; the binary path can't even ask). TIER0 ON (seeded shuffle + separate coverage noul): choices STAYED order-invariant (unroutable +1.000, material all_order 1.00) BUT two findings: (1) NEW — bonsai's coverage answer is ALWAYS 'claimable' (null_matrix fp=8/8, fpr=1.0): the production model has NO null sense, the separate question just measures that blindness precisely; (2) station_radius REGRESSED to -0.138: 2/8 wait_fallback parse failures (-2.00 each — the extra coverage JSON broke output shape on the edge scenario) + heavy reasoning-length penalties (right claim, budget-blown reasoning: +0.00/+0.17 rows); claimable-scenario mean off≈+0.95 vs on≈+0.56. VERDICT: Tier-0 factorization CONFIRMS order-invariant choices on the LLM path (JEVA hypothesis holds for choices) but is NOT a free win on bonsai — zero null discrimination + parse-reliability cost on edge scenarios; tier0 stays experimental/OFF, now evidence-backed rather than precautionary. This STRENGTHENS the kev-recalibration follow-up: kev's argmax was right on the same classes AND its coverage scores carry separable signal (0.47 vs 0.563) — exactly the component bonsai lacks. Metrics: corpus-bonsai-t0off-20261020-002806.jsonl + corpus-bonsai-t0on-20261020-004431.jsonl. Servers: kev stopped after Phase 1; LM Studio left running (user's). Phase 2b (in-game TestSidecar01 run) NOT yet done — next in the protocol.`\n\n## Referenced By","oldString":"Nothing committed — tree holds the full changeset.`\n\n## Referenced By","path":"/Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop/mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
